PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L08U6.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":8,"cefr":"B2a","unit":6,"theme":"Balance and Well-Being","essential_question":"How can we keep a healthy balance between work, rest and play?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS1","title":"If I Were Fifteen Again…: Verb Moods","objectives":["Students will be able to identify and use the five verb moods.","Students will be able to use the subjunctive \"were\" for unreal situations and the base form after verbs and adjectives of importance.","I can say \"If I were you, I would sleep earlier.\"","I can say \"The doctor recommended that every student spend an hour outdoors.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التعرف على صيغ الفعل الخمس واستخدامها.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام were للمواقف غير الحقيقية والمصدر بعد أفعال وصفات الأهمية.","أستطيع أن أقول If I were you, I would sleep earlier.","أستطيع أن أقول The doctor recommended that every student spend an hour outdoors."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"well-being","pos":"noun","ipa":"/wɛlˈbiɪŋ/","definition":"the state of being healthy, comfortable and happy","arabic":"جودة الحياة / الرفاه","example":"Sport and sleep are important for your well-being.","image_id":"GV-L08-U6-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS1-W01"},{"word":"balance","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbæləns/","definition":"a healthy situation in which different parts of life get the right amount of time","arabic":"توازن","example":"It's hard to find a balance between study and rest.","image_id":"GV-L08-U6-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS1-W02"},{"word":"stress","pos":"noun","ipa":"/strɛs/","definition":"a feeling of worry caused by difficult situations","arabic":"ضغط نفسي / توتر","example":"Exams can cause a lot of stress.","image_id":"GV-L08-U6-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS1-W03"},{"word":"routine","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ruˈtin/","definition":"the usual order in which you do things every day","arabic":"روتين","example":"A good morning routine helps me start the day well.","image_id":"GV-L08-U6-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"English verbs have moods that show the speaker's attitude. The indicative states facts or opinions: Teenagers need eight to ten hours of sleep. The interrogative asks questions: How many of you sleep less than seven hours? The imperative gives commands, instructions or advice (no subject): Drink water. Don't skip breakfast.\nThe conditional mood uses would / could / might for imaginary or uncertain situations: I would go to bed earlier. The subjunctive mood is used for situations that are not real or that are required or recommended. Use were (for all subjects) in unreal situations: If I were fifteen again… / as if I were sitting in a library.\nAfter verbs like recommend, suggest, insist, demand, require and adjectives like essential, important, vital + that, American English uses the base form of the verb – no -s, no past: The doctor recommended that every student spend (NOT spends) an hour outdoors. It is essential that your brain be given time to rest. The negative is not + base form: She insisted that we not use our phones.\nindicative = facts • interrogative = questions • imperative = commands/advice\nconditional = would / could / might + base verb\nsubjunctive (unreal): If I were…, I wish he were…, as if she were…\nsubjunctive (required): recommend / insist / essential that + base form (not + base)","examples":["Exercise improves your mood. (indicative)","Do you drink enough water? (interrogative)","Turn off your screen an hour before bed. (imperative)","I would feel less tired if I slept more. (conditional)","If I were you, I would take a short break. (subjunctive + conditional)","The nurse recommended that Lina drink more water.","It is vital that every athlete warm up before training.","The coach insisted that the players not train in the midday heat."],"common_errors":["✗ If I was you, I would sleep earlier. → ✓ If I were you, I would sleep earlier. (Unreal situation → were (formal American English).)","✗ The doctor recommended that he rests. → ✓ The doctor recommended that he rest. (After recommend that → base form.)","✗ It is important that she is on time. → ✓ It is important that she be on time. (After important that → base form be.)","✗ The coach insisted that we didn't skip the warm-up. → ✓ The coach insisted that we not skip the warm-up. (Negative subjunctive → not + base form.)"],"arabic":"صيغ الفعل تُظهر موقف المتكلم: الإخبار (حقيقة)، والاستفهام (سؤال)، والأمر (تعليمات أو نصيحة دون فاعل)، والشرط (would / could / might لمواقف متخيَّلة).\nصيغة الـ subjunctive للمواقف غير الحقيقية: If I were…، as if I were… (were مع كل الضمائر).\nوبعد أفعال مثل recommend وinsist وsuggest وصفات مثل essential وimportant + that نستخدم المصدر دون s: The doctor recommended that he rest.\nالنفي: that we not use. وهذه الصيغة شائعة في الكتابة الرسمية الأمريكية وتظهر في SAT."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “If I Were Fifteen Again…: Verb Moods”. Let’s learn verb moods: indicative (facts, statements), interrogative (questions), imperative (commands, advice), conditional (would / could / might for imaginary situations), subjunctive (were for unreal situations; base form after recommend / insist / essential that) together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U6-LS1 | If I Were Fifteen Again…: Verb Moods","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Well-Being Week”: Last month, our school held its first Well-Being Week. On Sunday morning, the counselor, Mr. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Last month, our school held its first Well-Being Week. On Sunday morning, the counselor, Mr.","visual":"Image GV-L08-U6-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"English verbs have moods that show the speaker's attitude. The indicative states facts or opinions: Teenagers need eight to ten hours of sleep. The interrogative asks questions: How many of you sleep less than seven hours? The imperative gives commands, instructions or advice (no subject): Drink water. Don't skip breakfast. The conditional mood uses would / could / might for imaginary or uncertain situations: I would go to bed earlier. The subjunctive mood is used for situations that are not real or that are required or recommended. Use were (for all subjects) in unreal situations: If I were fifteen again… / as if I were sitting in a library.","on_screen":"indicative = facts • interrogative = questions • imperative = commands/advice • conditional = would / could / might + base verb • subjunctive (unreal): If I were…, I wish he were…, as if she were…","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Exercise improves your mood. (indicative) Do you drink enough water? (interrogative) Turn off your screen an hour before bed. (imperative)","on_screen":"Exercise improves your mood. (indicative) / Do you drink enough water? (interrogative) / Turn off your screen an hour before bed. (imperative)","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “If I was you, I would sleep earlier.” That’s not right. We say: “If I were you, I would sleep earlier.” Unreal situation → were (formal American English).","on_screen":"✗ If I was you, I would sleep earlier.   ✓ If I were you, I would sleep earlier.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"If I were fifteen again\" – is the speaker fifteen? … Think! … No – it's an unreal situation. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"If I were you, I would sleep earlier.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"If I were you, I would sleep earlier.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: verb moods: indicative (facts, statements), interrogative (questions), imperative (commands, advice), conditional (would / could / might for imaginary situations), subjunctive (were for unreal situations; base form after recommend / insist / essential that).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","صيغ الفعل تُظهر موقف المتكلم: الإخبار (حقيقة)، والاستفهام (سؤال)، والأمر (تعليمات أو نصيحة دون فاعل)، والشرط (would / could / might لمواقف متخيَّلة).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: If I was you, I would sleep earlier. — الصحيح: If I were you, I would sleep earlier.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول If I were you, I would sleep earlier."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Well-Being Week","body":"Last month, our school held its first Well-Being Week. On Sunday morning, the counselor, Mr. Khalid, stood on the stage and asked a simple question: \"How many of you sleep less than seven hours a night?\" Almost every hand went up.\n\"Take care of your body and mind,\" he said. \"Don't skip breakfast, and drink water throughout the day.\" Then he explained that teenagers need between eight and ten hours of sleep. \"If I were fifteen again,\" he joked, \"I would go to bed before my phone did!\"\nDuring the week, doctors from a local hospital visited our classes. One of them recommended that every student spend at least an hour outdoors each day. Another insisted that we not use our phones in the hour before bed. \"It is essential that your brain be given time to rest,\" she explained.\nOn Wednesday, we tried mindfulness for the first time. At first, my friend Saad laughed. \"I feel as if I were sitting in a library with my eyes closed,\" he whispered. But by the end of the session, even he looked calmer.\nOn the last day, Mr. Khalid asked us to make one small change. I promised to keep my phone outside my bedroom. If I had known how much better I would feel, I would have done it years ago!","word_count":221,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"If I ___ you, I would go to bed earlier.","options":["will be","am","were","was being"],"answer":"were","explanation":"Subjunctive were – unreal situation.","explanation_ar":"were للمواقف غير الحقيقية."},{"q":"The doctor recommended that every student ___ at least an hour outdoors.","options":["spends","spent","will spend","spend"],"answer":"spend","explanation":"Subjunctive base form after recommend / essential that.","explanation_ar":"المصدر بعد recommend that."},{"q":"\"___ skip breakfast,\" the counselor said.","options":["You don't","Don't","Not","No"],"answer":"Don't","explanation":"Imperative – a command or advice.","explanation_ar":"الأمر."},{"q":"It is essential that your brain ___ given time to rest.","options":["being","is","was","be"],"answer":"be","explanation":"Subjunctive base form after recommend / essential that.","explanation_ar":"المصدر بعد recommend that."},{"q":"Which sentence is in the conditional mood?","options":["I feel calmer after I meditate.","Do you feel calmer?","I would feel calmer if I meditated.","Feel calmer by meditating."],"answer":"I would feel calmer if I meditated.","explanation":"Conditional – would / could / might.","explanation_ar":"الشرط."},{"q":"Sleep experts recommend that teenagers ______ between eight and ten hours each night to support their memory and concentration.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["get","getting","got","gets"],"answer":"get","explanation":"Subjunctive base form after recommend / essential that.","explanation_ar":"المصدر بعد recommend that."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the correct form. Word bank: were, indicative, subjunctive, drink, not train, interrogative","items":[{"q":"If Saad ______ (be) more organized, he wouldn't feel so stressed.","options":[],"answer":"were","explanation":"Subjunctive were – unreal situation.","explanation_ar":"were للمواقف غير الحقيقية."},{"q":"The coach insisted that the team ______ (not / train) in the midday heat.","options":[],"answer":"not train","explanation":"Subjunctive base form after recommend / essential that.","explanation_ar":"المصدر بعد recommend that."},{"q":"The nurse suggested that Lina ______ (drink) more water.","options":[],"answer":"drink","explanation":"Subjunctive base form after recommend / essential that.","explanation_ar":"المصدر بعد recommend that."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS1-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Name the mood: indicative, interrogative, imperative, conditional or subjunctive. Word bank: were, indicative, subjunctive, drink, not train, interrogative","items":[{"q":"Exercise improves your mood. → ______","options":[],"answer":"indicative","explanation":"Indicative – a fact or statement.","explanation_ar":"الإخبار."},{"q":"Do you get enough sleep? → ______","options":[],"answer":"interrogative","explanation":"Interrogative – a question.","explanation_ar":"الاستفهام."},{"q":"I wish I were less tired. → ______","options":[],"answer":"subjunctive","explanation":"Subjunctive were – unreal situation.","explanation_ar":"were للمواقف غير الحقيقية."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Give advice in different moods.","items":[{"q":"Give advice with an imperative: ___","options":[],"answer":"Take a ten-minute walk after lunch.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb moods: indicative (facts, statements), interrogative (questions), imperative (commands, advice), conditional (would / could / might for imaginary situations), subjunctive (were for unreal situations; base form after recommend / insist / essential that) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Give advice with \"If I were you, …\": ___","options":[],"answer":"If I were you, I'd put my phone in another room while studying.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb moods: indicative (facts, statements), interrogative (questions), imperative (commands, advice), conditional (would / could / might for imaginary situations), subjunctive (were for unreal situations; base form after recommend / insist / essential that) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a recommendation with \"It is important that…\": ___","options":[],"answer":"It is important that every student eat a healthy breakfast.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb moods: indicative (facts, statements), interrogative (questions), imperative (commands, advice), conditional (would / could / might for imaginary situations), subjunctive (were for unreal situations; base form after recommend / insist / essential that) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"as if\" + were: ___","options":[],"answer":"My little brother acts as if he were the boss of the house.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb moods: indicative (facts, statements), interrogative (questions), imperative (commands, advice), conditional (would / could / might for imaginary situations), subjunctive (were for unreal situations; base form after recommend / insist / essential that) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask a question about someone's routine: ___","options":[],"answer":"How many hours do you spend outdoors each week?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb moods: indicative (facts, statements), interrogative (questions), imperative (commands, advice), conditional (would / could / might for imaginary situations), subjunctive (were for unreal situations; base form after recommend / insist / essential that) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Well-being poster.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 imperative tips for a healthy school day.","options":[],"answer":"Drink water every hour. Stand up and stretch between lessons. Don't eat too many sweets.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb moods: indicative (facts, statements), interrogative (questions), imperative (commands, advice), conditional (would / could / might for imaginary situations), subjunctive (were for unreal situations; base form after recommend / insist / essential that) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 recommendations with the subjunctive (recommend / insist / essential that).","options":[],"answer":"The school nurse recommends that students sleep at least eight hours. It is essential that everyone wear a hat in the sun.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb moods: indicative (facts, statements), interrogative (questions), imperative (commands, advice), conditional (would / could / might for imaginary situations), subjunctive (were for unreal situations; base form after recommend / insist / essential that) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one conditional sentence about a change you would make.","options":[],"answer":"If I had more free time, I would join the swimming club.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb moods: indicative (facts, statements), interrogative (questions), imperative (commands, advice), conditional (would / could / might for imaginary situations), subjunctive (were for unreal situations; base form after recommend / insist / essential that) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Ball Toss Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Students stand in a circle. The teacher says a cue word and throws the ball.","The catcher makes a sentence with the cue word and verb moods: indicative (facts, statements), interrogative (questions), imperative (commands, advice), conditional (would / could / might for imaginary situations), subjunctive (were for unreal situations; base form after recommend / insist / essential that).","If it is correct, the catcher chooses the next cue word and throws the ball to a new student.","If it is not correct, classmates help fix it, and the same student tries again."],"data":[{"label":"If I were you, I'd…"},{"label":"I wish I were…"},{"label":"The doctor recommended that he…"},{"label":"It is essential that she…"},{"label":"Take…"},{"label":"Don't…"},{"label":"as if he were…"},{"label":"insisted that we not…"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I wish I ___ more relaxed before exams.","options":["were","been","will be","am"],"answer":"were","explanation":"Subjunctive were – unreal situation.","explanation_ar":"were للمواقف غير الحقيقية."},{"q":"The dentist insisted that my brother ___ his teeth twice a day.","options":["brushes","brushed","brush","is brushing"],"answer":"brush","explanation":"Subjunctive base form after recommend / essential that.","explanation_ar":"المصدر بعد recommend that."},{"q":"\"___ your water bottle!\" the coach shouted.","options":["Brings","To bring","You bring","Bring"],"answer":"Bring","explanation":"Imperative – a command or advice.","explanation_ar":"الأمر."},{"q":"","options":["It is vital that every runner will warm up first.","It is vital that every runner warms up first.","It is vital that every runner warmed up first.","It is vital that every runner warm up first."],"answer":"It is vital that every runner warm up first.","explanation":"Subjunctive base form after recommend / essential that.","explanation_ar":"المصدر بعد recommend that."},{"q":"Which sentence is in the interrogative mood?","options":["I exercise three times a week.","If I exercised more, I'd feel better.","How often do you exercise?","Exercise three times a week."],"answer":"How often do you exercise?","explanation":"Interrogative – a question.","explanation_ar":"الاستفهام."},{"q":"Which sentence is in the indicative mood?","options":["Fresh air improves concentration.","If only I had more fresh air!","Get some fresh air.","I'd feel better with fresh air."],"answer":"Fresh air improves concentration.","explanation":"Indicative – a fact or statement.","explanation_ar":"الإخبار."},{"q":"He talks as if he ___ a doctor, but he's still at school.","options":["will be","been","were","is being"],"answer":"were","explanation":"Subjunctive were – unreal situation.","explanation_ar":"were للمواقف غير الحقيقية."},{"q":"If we had more time outdoors, we ___ healthier.","options":["will be","would be","are","were being"],"answer":"would be","explanation":"Conditional – would / could / might.","explanation_ar":"الشرط."},{"q":"The school's new policy requires that every student ______ a short physical activity break between morning lessons.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["take","took","takes","is taking"],"answer":"take","explanation":"Subjunctive base form after recommend / essential that.","explanation_ar":"المصدر بعد recommend that."},{"q":"After running the marathon, the athlete looked as though she ______ ready to run another one.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["are","were","have been","was being"],"answer":"were","explanation":"Subjunctive were – unreal situation.","explanation_ar":"were للمواقف غير الحقيقية."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"A school stage with a banner \"Well-Being Week\"; Mr. Khalid the counselor speaking to students; posters with icons for sleep (moon), water (bottle), outdoor time (sun) and mindfulness (calm face); Saad sitting cross-legged with eyes closed during a mindfulness session. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A school stage with a banner \"Well-Being Week\"; Mr. Khalid the counselor speaking to students; posters with icons for sleep (moon), water (bottle), outdoor time (sun) and mindfulness (calm face); Saad sitting cross-legged with eyes closed during a mindfulness session"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about verb moods: indicative (facts, statements), interrogative (questions), imperative (commands, advice), conditional (would / could / might for imaginary situations), subjunctive (were for unreal situations; base form after recommend / insist / essential that), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about verb moods: indicative (facts, statements), interrogative (questions), imperative (commands, advice), conditional (would / could / might for imaginary situations), subjunctive (were for unreal situations"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows well-being (the state of being healthy, comfortable and happy); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing well-being: the state of being healthy, comfortable and happy"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows balance (a healthy situation in which different parts of life get the right amount of time); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing balance: a healthy situation in which different parts of life get the right amount of time"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows stress (a feeling of worry caused by difficult situations); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing stress: a feeling of worry caused by difficult situations"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows routine (the usual order in which you do things every day); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing routine: the usual order in which you do things every day"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Ball Toss Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Ball Toss Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS1-W01","script":"well-being. well-being. Sport and sleep are important for your well-being.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS1-W02","script":"balance. balance. It's hard to find a balance between study and rest.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS1-W03","script":"stress. stress. Exams can cause a lot of stress.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS1-W04","script":"routine. routine. A good morning routine helps me start the day well.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS1-T1","script":"Last month, our school held its first Well-Being Week. On Sunday morning, the counselor, Mr. Khalid, stood on the stage and asked a simple question: \"How many of you sleep less than seven hours a night?\" Almost every hand went up. \"Take care of your body and mind,\" he said. \"Don't skip breakfast, and drink water throughout the day.\" Then he explained that teenagers need between eight and ten hours of sleep. \"If I were fifteen again,\" he joked, \"I would go to bed before my phone did!\" During the week, doctors from a local hospital visited our classes. One of them recommended that every student spend at least an hour outdoors each day. Another insisted that we not use our phones in the hour before bed. \"It is essential that your brain be given time to rest,\" she explained. On Wednesday, we tried mindfulness for the first time. At first, my friend Saad laughed. \"I feel as if I were sitting in a library with my eyes closed,\" he whispered. But by the end of the session, even he looked calmer. On the last day, Mr. Khalid asked us to make one small change. I promised to keep my phone outside my bedroom. If I had known how much better I would feel, I would have done it years ago!","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “If I Were Fifteen Again…: Verb Moods”. Let’s learn verb moods: indicative (facts, statements), interrogative (questions), imperative (commands, advice), conditional (would / could / might for imaginary situations), subjunctive (were for unreal situations; base form after recommend / insist / essential that) together. Listen to the start of “Well-Being Week”: Last month, our school held its first Well-Being Week. On Sunday morning, the counselor, Mr. Look at the green words. English verbs have moods that show the speaker's attitude. The indicative states facts or opinions: Teenagers need eight to ten hours of sleep. The interrogative asks questions: How many of you sleep less than seven hours? The imperative gives commands, instructions or advice (no subject): Drink water. Don't skip breakfast. The conditional mood uses would / could / might for imaginary or uncertain situations: I would go to bed earlier. The subjunctive mood is used for situations that are not real or that are required or recommended. Use were (for all subjects) in unreal situations: If I were fifteen again… / as if I were sitting in a library. Here are some examples. Exercise improves your mood. (indicative) Do you drink enough water? (interrogative) Turn off your screen an hour before bed. (imperative) Be careful! Some learners say: “If I was you, I would sleep earlier.” That’s not right. We say: “If I were you, I would sleep earlier.” Unreal situation → were (formal American English). Quick check: \"If I were fifteen again\" – is the speaker fifteen? … Think! … No – it's an unreal situation. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"If I were you, I would sleep earlier.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS2","title":"The Doctor Recommended That He Rest: The Subjunctive in Depth","objectives":["Students will be able to use the subjunctive after verbs and adjectives of importance in formal recommendations.","Students will be able to choose between the subjunctive, -ing forms and infinitives after suggest, recommend and insist.","I can write \"It is essential that every student be on time.\"","I can write \"She suggested taking a break\" and \"She suggested that we take a break.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام صيغة الـ subjunctive بعد أفعال وصفات الأهمية في التوصيات الرسمية.","سيتمكن الطلاب من الاختيار بين الـ subjunctive وصيغة ing والمصدر بعد suggest وrecommend وinsist.","أستطيع أن أكتب It is essential that every student be on time.","أستطيع أن أكتب She suggested taking a break وShe suggested that we take a break."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"nutrition","pos":"noun","ipa":"/nuˈtrɪʃən/","definition":"the food you eat and how it affects your health","arabic":"التغذية","example":"Good nutrition gives you energy to learn.","image_id":"GV-L08-U6-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS2-W01"},{"word":"hydrated","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈhaɪˌdreɪtəd/","definition":"having enough water in your body","arabic":"رطب / يشرب كفايته من الماء","example":"Stay hydrated, especially in summer.","image_id":"GV-L08-U6-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS2-W02"},{"word":"sedentary","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈsɛdənˌtɛri/","definition":"spending a lot of time sitting and not moving much","arabic":"قليل الحركة / خامل","example":"A sedentary lifestyle can lead to health problems.","image_id":"GV-L08-U6-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS2-W03"},{"word":"posture","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɑstʃɚ/","definition":"the way you hold your body when you sit or stand","arabic":"وضعية الجسم","example":"Sit up straight; good posture protects your back.","image_id":"GV-L08-U6-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"The mandative subjunctive is used in formal recommendations, rules and demands. Pattern 1: verb + that + subject + base form: The doctor recommended that he rest. The coach insisted that everyone arrive on time. Verbs: recommend, suggest, insist, demand, require, propose, request, ask, urge.\nPattern 2: It is + adjective + that + subject + base form: It is essential that every student be hydrated. Adjectives: essential, vital, important, necessary, crucial, urgent, critical. The base form never changes: no -s (he rest), no past (he rest, even after recommended), and be for all subjects. Negative: that he not eat late. Passive: that the rules be followed.\nAlternatives: suggest / recommend + -ing: She suggested taking a break. ask / urge / advise + person + to: She advised me to rest. Don't mix patterns: (not: She suggested me to rest.) → She suggested that I rest. / She suggested resting. Remember the were-subjunctive too: I wish I were fitter; If he were less busy…\nrecommend / insist / suggest + that + subject + base form\nIt is essential / vital / important + that + subject + base form\nnegative: that he not + base • passive: that it be + past participle\nsuggest + -ing • advise / urge + person + to • NOT suggest me to","examples":["The nurse recommended that Adam see an eye doctor.","It is crucial that the patient not lift anything heavy.","The principal insisted that the new rules be followed.","Our coach suggested that each player keep a sleep diary.","It is vital that children be protected from the sun.","The doctor suggested cutting down on sugar.","My father urged me to take a break from my screen.","The report proposes that schools start later in the morning."],"common_errors":["✗ The doctor recommended that he rests at home. → ✓ The doctor recommended that he rest at home. (Base form – no -s.)","✗ It is essential that she is on time. → ✓ It is essential that she be on time. (be for all subjects.)","✗ She suggested me to take a break. → ✓ She suggested that I take a break. / She suggested taking a break. (suggest doesn't take person + to.)","✗ The coach insisted that we didn't eat junk food. → ✓ The coach insisted that we not eat junk food. (Negative subjunctive → not + base.)"],"arabic":"صيغة الـ subjunctive الإلزامية تُستخدم في التوصيات والقواعد الرسمية: فعل (recommend / insist / suggest) + that + فاعل + المصدر: The doctor recommended that he rest.\nأو It is + صفة (essential / vital / important) + that + فاعل + المصدر: It is essential that every student be hydrated.\nالمصدر لا يتغيّر: لا s ولا ماضٍ، وbe مع كل الفواعل، والنفي not + المصدر، والمجهول be + التصريف الثالث.\nالبدائل: suggest + ing، وadvise / urge + الشخص + to. ولا نقول suggested me to."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Doctor Recommended That He Rest: The Subjunctive in Depth”. Let’s learn mandative subjunctive after verbs (recommend, suggest, insist, demand, require, propose, ask) and adjectives (essential, vital, important, necessary, crucial) + that + base form; negative not + base form; passive be + past participle; alternatives with -ing (suggest taking) and infinitives; were-subjunctive after wish, if, as if together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U6-LS2 | The Doctor Recommended That He Rest: The Subjunctive in Depth","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: The trainer suggested that we stretch after running. It is important that you not skip meals. Did the doctor recommend that he stay home?","on_screen":"The trainer suggested that we stretch after running. | It is important that you not skip meals. | Did the doctor recommend that he stay home?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"The mandative subjunctive is used in formal recommendations, rules and demands. Pattern 1: verb + that + subject + base form: The doctor recommended that he rest. The coach insisted that everyone arrive on time. Verbs: recommend, suggest, insist, demand, require, propose, request, ask, urge. Pattern 2: It is + adjective + that + subject + base form: It is essential that every student be hydrated. Adjectives: essential, vital, important, necessary, crucial, urgent, critical. The base form never changes: no -s (he rest), no past (he rest, even after recommended), and be for all subjects. Negative: that he not eat late. Passive: that the rules be followed.","on_screen":"recommend / insist / suggest + that + subject + base form • It is essential / vital / important + that + subject + base form • negative: that he not + base • passive: that it be + past participle","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The nurse recommended that Adam see an eye doctor. It is crucial that the patient not lift anything heavy. The principal insisted that the new rules be followed.","on_screen":"The nurse recommended that Adam see an eye doctor. / It is crucial that the patient not lift anything heavy. / The principal insisted that the new rules be followed.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The doctor recommended that he rests at home.” That’s not right. We say: “The doctor recommended that he rest at home.” Base form – no -s.","on_screen":"✗ The doctor recommended that he rests at home.   ✓ The doctor recommended that he rest at home.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"The doctor recommended that he rest.\" Is \"rest\" a mistake? … Think! … No – it's the subjunctive (base form). Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"It is essential that every student be on time.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"It is essential that every student be on time.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: mandative subjunctive after verbs (recommend, suggest, insist, demand, require, propose, ask) and adjectives (essential, vital, important, necessary, crucial) + that + base form; negative not + base form; passive be + past participle; alternatives with -ing (suggest taking) and infinitives; were-subjunctive after wish, if, as if.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","صيغة الـ subjunctive الإلزامية تُستخدم في التوصيات والقواعد الرسمية: فعل (recommend / insist / suggest) + that + فاعل + المصدر: The doctor recommended that he rest.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The doctor recommended that he rests at home. — الصحيح: The doctor recommended that he rest at home.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب It is essential that every student be on time."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"The doctor recommended that Faisal ___ for two weeks.","options":["rested","is resting","rests","rest"],"answer":"rest","explanation":"verb + that + base form (recommend, insist).","explanation_ar":"الفعل + that + المصدر."},{"q":"It is essential that every athlete ___ hydrated during the race.","options":["being","was","be","is"],"answer":"be","explanation":"It is + adjective + that + base form.","explanation_ar":"الصفة + that + المصدر."},{"q":"The coach insisted that the players ___ energy drinks before matches.","options":["don't drink","didn't drink","not drink","not drinking"],"answer":"not drink","explanation":"Negative subjunctive: not + base form.","explanation_ar":"النفي."},{"q":"The principal demanded that the new safety rules ___ followed.","options":["being","be","were","are"],"answer":"be","explanation":"Passive subjunctive: be + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المجهول."},{"q":"","options":["The trainer suggested stretching after every run.","The trainer suggested that we stretching after every run.","The trainer suggested us to stretch after every run.","The trainer suggested to stretch after every run."],"answer":"The trainer suggested stretching after every run.","explanation":"suggest + -ing / advise + person + to.","explanation_ar":"البدائل."},{"q":"To reduce eye strain, optometrists suggest that people who work at computers ______ every twenty minutes to look at something far away.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["pause","pausing","pauses","paused"],"answer":"pause","explanation":"verb + that + base form (recommend, insist).","explanation_ar":"الفعل + that + المصدر."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the subjunctive. Word bank: be checked, bring, not skip","items":[{"q":"It is important that you ______ (not / skip) breakfast before an exam.","options":[],"answer":"not skip","explanation":"Negative subjunctive: not + base form.","explanation_ar":"النفي."},{"q":"The nurse requested that each student ______ (bring) a water bottle.","options":[],"answer":"bring","explanation":"verb + that + base form (recommend, insist).","explanation_ar":"الفعل + that + المصدر."},{"q":"It is vital that the injury ______ (check – passive) by a doctor.","options":[],"answer":"be checked","explanation":"Passive subjunctive: be + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المجهول."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite the sentences with the word in brackets.","items":[{"q":"The doctor said, \"You should rest.\" (recommended that)  (subjunctive)","options":[],"answer":"The doctor recommended that I rest.","explanation":"verb + that + base form (recommend, insist).","explanation_ar":"الفعل + that + المصدر."},{"q":"It's important for everyone to wear a helmet. (It is important that)  (subjunctive)","options":[],"answer":"It is important that everyone wear a helmet.","explanation":"It is + adjective + that + base form.","explanation_ar":"الصفة + that + المصدر."},{"q":"She said, \"Let's take a walk.\" (suggested + -ing)","options":[],"answer":"She suggested taking a walk.","explanation":"suggest + -ing / advise + person + to.","explanation_ar":"البدائل."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Give formal recommendations.","items":[{"q":"A recommendation from a doctor about sleep: ___","options":[],"answer":"The doctor recommends that teenagers sleep at least eight hours.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mandative subjunctive after verbs (recommend, suggest, insist, demand, require, propose, ask) and adjectives (essential, vital, important, necessary, crucial) + that + base form; negative not + base form; passive be + past participle; alternatives with -ing (suggest taking) and infinitives; were-subjunctive after wish, if, as if correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A school rule with \"It is essential that…\": ___","options":[],"answer":"It is essential that every student wear a hat during outdoor lessons.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mandative subjunctive after verbs (recommend, suggest, insist, demand, require, propose, ask) and adjectives (essential, vital, important, necessary, crucial) + that + base form; negative not + base form; passive be + past participle; alternatives with -ing (suggest taking) and infinitives; were-subjunctive after wish, if, as if correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A demand with \"insist that… not\": ___","options":[],"answer":"My mother insists that I not use my phone at dinner.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mandative subjunctive after verbs (recommend, suggest, insist, demand, require, propose, ask) and adjectives (essential, vital, important, necessary, crucial) + that + base form; negative not + base form; passive be + past participle; alternatives with -ing (suggest taking) and infinitives; were-subjunctive after wish, if, as if correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A suggestion with \"suggest + -ing\": ___","options":[],"answer":"I suggest walking to school when the weather is cool.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mandative subjunctive after verbs (recommend, suggest, insist, demand, require, propose, ask) and adjectives (essential, vital, important, necessary, crucial) + that + base form; negative not + base form; passive be + past participle; alternatives with -ing (suggest taking) and infinitives; were-subjunctive after wish, if, as if correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A wish with \"were\": ___","options":[],"answer":"I wish my school day were a little shorter.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mandative subjunctive after verbs (recommend, suggest, insist, demand, require, propose, ask) and adjectives (essential, vital, important, necessary, crucial) + that + base form; negative not + base form; passive be + past participle; alternatives with -ing (suggest taking) and infinitives; were-subjunctive after wish, if, as if correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Healthy school proposal.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 recommendations for a healthier school using the subjunctive.","options":[],"answer":"We recommend that the school start at 8 a.m. It is important that every class have a five-minute movement break. We propose that the canteen sell more fruit.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mandative subjunctive after verbs (recommend, suggest, insist, demand, require, propose, ask) and adjectives (essential, vital, important, necessary, crucial) + that + base form; negative not + base form; passive be + past participle; alternatives with -ing (suggest taking) and infinitives; were-subjunctive after wish, if, as if correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with \"advise/urge + person + to\".","options":[],"answer":"Doctors advise students to drink water regularly. Our coach urges us to stretch every day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mandative subjunctive after verbs (recommend, suggest, insist, demand, require, propose, ask) and adjectives (essential, vital, important, necessary, crucial) + that + base form; negative not + base form; passive be + past participle; alternatives with -ing (suggest taking) and infinitives; were-subjunctive after wish, if, as if correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with a passive subjunctive.","options":[],"answer":"It is vital that the water fountains be cleaned every day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mandative subjunctive after verbs (recommend, suggest, insist, demand, require, propose, ask) and adjectives (essential, vital, important, necessary, crucial) + that + base form; negative not + base form; passive be + past participle; alternatives with -ing (suggest taking) and infinitives; were-subjunctive after wish, if, as if correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Dice Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Turn over a cue card and roll the die.","Make a sentence with the cue in the form shown by the die.","The player on the left checks; a correct sentence wins the card.","The player with the most cards after 7 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"I / you / sleep earlier (If I were)"},{"cue":"the doctor / recommend / he / rest (that he rest)"},{"cue":"it / be / essential / she / drink water"},{"cue":"the coach / insist / we / not / skip the warm-up"},{"cue":"I wish / I / be / less tired"},{"cue":"he / look / as if / he / be / exhausted"},{"cue":"the counselor / suggest / they / take breaks"},{"cue":"drink / water (imperative)"},{"cue":"not / skip / breakfast (imperative)"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The physiotherapist suggested that Hamad ___ his back straight while studying.","options":["is keeping","kept","keeps","keep"],"answer":"keep","explanation":"verb + that + base form (recommend, insist).","explanation_ar":"الفعل + that + المصدر."},{"q":"It is crucial that the patient ___ to the hospital immediately.","options":["goes","go","going","went"],"answer":"go","explanation":"It is + adjective + that + base form.","explanation_ar":"الصفة + that + المصدر."},{"q":"The coach asked that we ___ late for training again.","options":["aren't","not being","not be","weren't"],"answer":"not be","explanation":"Negative subjunctive: not + base form.","explanation_ar":"النفي."},{"q":"It is necessary that all medicines ___ out of children's reach.","options":["keeping","are kept","be kept","were kept"],"answer":"be kept","explanation":"Passive subjunctive: be + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المجهول."},{"q":"","options":["My doctor suggested me to cut down on sugar.","My doctor advised that me cut down on sugar.","My doctor advised me cutting down on sugar.","My doctor advised me to cut down on sugar."],"answer":"My doctor advised me to cut down on sugar.","explanation":"suggest + -ing / advise + person + to.","explanation_ar":"البدائل."},{"q":"","options":["The report recommends schools to starting later.","The report recommends that schools start later.","The report recommends that schools starts later.","The report recommends that schools started later."],"answer":"The report recommends that schools start later.","explanation":"verb + that + base form (recommend, insist).","explanation_ar":"الفعل + that + المصدر."},{"q":"I wish my little brother ___ more patient with me.","options":["is","will be","been","were"],"answer":"were","explanation":"were after wish / if / as if.","explanation_ar":"were."},{"q":"It is important that everyone ___ kind to themselves during stressful times.","options":["be","is","are","being"],"answer":"be","explanation":"It is + adjective + that + base form.","explanation_ar":"الصفة + that + المصدر."},{"q":"Because heat stroke can be dangerous, health officials urge that outdoor workers ______ during the hottest hours of the day.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["rest","rested","resting","rests"],"answer":"rest","explanation":"verb + that + base form (recommend, insist).","explanation_ar":"الفعل + that + المصدر."},{"q":"The safety guidelines require that every swimming pool ______ by a qualified lifeguard whenever it is open.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["was supervised","be supervised","supervising","is supervised"],"answer":"be supervised","explanation":"Passive subjunctive: be + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المجهول."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A school clinic: the nurse writing a recommendation card (\"It is important that you drink 8 glasses of water\"), a student with a sports injury and a coach reading a doctor's note \"The doctor recommends that he rest for two weeks\". Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A school clinic: the nurse writing a recommendation card (\"It is important that you drink 8 glasses of water\"), a student with a sports injury and a coach reading a doctor's note \"The doctor recommends that he rest for two weeks\""},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of mandative subjunctive after verbs (recommend, suggest, insist, demand, require, propose, ask) and adjectives (essential, vital, important, necessary, crucial) + that + base form; negative not + base form; passive be + past participle; alternatives with -ing (suggest taking) and infinitives; were-subjunctive after wish, if, as if: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Balance and Well-Being”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of mandative subjunctive after verbs (recommend, suggest, insist, demand, require, propose, ask) and adjectives (essential, vital, important, necessary, crucial) + that + base form"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows nutrition (the food you eat and how it affects your health); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing nutrition: the food you eat and how it affects your health"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows hydrated (having enough water in your body); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing hydrated: having enough water in your body"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows sedentary (spending a lot of time sitting and not moving much); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing sedentary: spending a lot of time sitting and not moving much"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows posture (the way you hold your body when you sit or stand); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing posture: the way you hold your body when you sit or stand"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Dice Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Dice Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS2-W01","script":"nutrition. nutrition. Good nutrition gives you energy to learn.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS2-W02","script":"hydrated. hydrated. Stay hydrated, especially in summer.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS2-W03","script":"sedentary. sedentary. A sedentary lifestyle can lead to health problems.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS2-W04","script":"posture. posture. Sit up straight; good posture protects your back.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Doctor Recommended That He Rest: The Subjunctive in Depth”. Let’s learn mandative subjunctive after verbs (recommend, suggest, insist, demand, require, propose, ask) and adjectives (essential, vital, important, necessary, crucial) + that + base form; negative not + base form; passive be + past participle; alternatives with -ing (suggest taking) and infinitives; were-subjunctive after wish, if, as if together. Remember these patterns: The trainer suggested that we stretch after running. It is important that you not skip meals. Did the doctor recommend that he stay home? The mandative subjunctive is used in formal recommendations, rules and demands. Pattern 1: verb + that + subject + base form: The doctor recommended that he rest. The coach insisted that everyone arrive on time. Verbs: recommend, suggest, insist, demand, require, propose, request, ask, urge. Pattern 2: It is + adjective + that + subject + base form: It is essential that every student be hydrated. Adjectives: essential, vital, important, necessary, crucial, urgent, critical. The base form never changes: no -s (he rest), no past (he rest, even after recommended), and be for all subjects. Negative: that he not eat late. Passive: that the rules be followed. Here are some examples. The nurse recommended that Adam see an eye doctor. It is crucial that the patient not lift anything heavy. The principal insisted that the new rules be followed. Be careful! Some learners say: “The doctor recommended that he rests at home.” That’s not right. We say: “The doctor recommended that he rest at home.” Base form – no -s. Quick check: \"The doctor recommended that he rest.\" Is \"rest\" a mistake? … Think! … No – it's the subjunctive (base form). Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"It is essential that every student be on time.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3","title":"Recharge Your Batteries: Well-Being Idioms and Phrasal Verbs","objectives":["Students will be able to interpret well-being idioms in context.","Students will be able to use phrasal verbs about health and balance accurately.","I can explain \"burn the midnight oil\" and \"recharge your batteries\".","I can say \"I'm cutting down on sugar\" and \"I wind down by reading.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تفسير التعابير الاصطلاحية عن جودة الحياة في السياق.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام الأفعال المركبة عن الصحة والتوازن بدقة.","أستطيع أن أشرح burn the midnight oil وrecharge your batteries.","أستطيع أن أقول I'm cutting down on sugar وI wind down by reading."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"mindfulness","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmaɪndfəlnəs/","definition":"the practice of paying calm attention to the present moment","arabic":"اليقظة الذهنية","example":"Mindfulness can help you feel calmer before a test.","image_id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS3-W01"},{"word":"burnout","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbɝˌnaʊt/","definition":"extreme tiredness caused by working too hard for too long","arabic":"الإنهاك / الاحتراق الوظيفي","example":"Too much work and too little rest can lead to burnout.","image_id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS3-W02"},{"word":"moderation","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌmɑdɚˈeɪʃən/","definition":"not doing too much or too little of something","arabic":"الاعتدال","example":"Enjoy sweets in moderation.","image_id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS3-W03"},{"word":"fatigue","pos":"noun","ipa":"/fəˈtiɡ/","definition":"a feeling of being extremely tired","arabic":"إرهاق","example":"Lack of sleep causes fatigue and poor concentration.","image_id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS3-W04"},{"word":"cope","pos":"verb","ipa":"/koʊp/","definition":"to deal successfully with a difficult situation","arabic":"يتكيّف / يتعامل مع","example":"She coped well with the pressure of the competition.","image_id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS3-W05"},{"word":"unwind","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ənˈwaɪnd/","definition":"to relax after a period of work or worry","arabic":"يسترخي","example":"I unwind by reading before bed.","image_id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-W06","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS3-W06"},{"word":"overwhelmed","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌoʊvɚˈwɛlmd/","definition":"feeling that you have too much to deal with","arabic":"مُثقَل / مغمور","example":"He felt overwhelmed by all his homework.","image_id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-W07","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS3-W07"}],"explanation":{"text":"Idioms are phrases whose meaning is different from the meanings of the individual words. Feel under the weather = feel a little sick. Burn the midnight oil = study or work late at night. Recharge your batteries = rest to get your energy back. Be on top of the world = feel extremely happy. Keep your cool = stay calm. Let off steam = release energy or anger through activity. Run out of steam = lose energy. Take it easy = relax.\nPhrasal verbs about well-being: wind down (relax after activity), cut down on (reduce), cut out (stop completely), work out (exercise), burn out (become exhausted from overwork), bounce back (recover quickly), calm down, take up (start a new hobby), switch off (stop thinking about work; turn off a device).\nIdioms are often informal, so use them in conversation, stories and friendly letters—not in formal reports. Learn them as whole phrases: we say burn the midnight oil, not (not: burn the night oil).\nCollocations/phrases: feel under the weather • burn the midnight oil • recharge your batteries • on top of the world | keep your cool • let off steam • run out of steam • take it easy | wind down • cut down on • cut out • work out | burn out • bounce back • take up • switch off","examples":["I'm feeling under the weather, so I'll stay home today.","Don't burn the midnight oil before the exam—sleep instead.","A weekend in the mountains helped me recharge my batteries.","When our team won, I was on top of the world.","My father works out at the gym three times a week.","I'm cutting down on fizzy drinks.","After losing the first match, the team bounced back and won the cup.","I wind down by reading a few pages before bed."],"common_errors":["✗ I studied until 2 a.m. – I burned the night oil. → ✓ I burned the midnight oil. (Fixed idiom: the midnight oil.)","✗ I'm cutting down sugar. → ✓ I'm cutting down on sugar. (cut down on + noun.)","✗ He did a work out at the gym. → ✓ He worked out at the gym. / He did a workout. (Verb work out; noun workout.)","✗ Calm you down! → ✓ Calm down! (calm down (no object for yourself).)"],"arabic":"التعابير الاصطلاحية معناها مختلف عن معاني كلماتها: under the weather (متوعّك قليلًا)، burn the midnight oil (يسهر للدراسة أو العمل)، recharge your batteries (يستعيد طاقته).\non top of the world (في غاية السعادة)، keep your cool (يحافظ على هدوئه)، let off steam (يُفرّغ طاقته أو غضبه).\nأفعال مركبة: wind down (يسترخي)، cut down on (يقلّل من)، work out (يتمرّن)، burn out (يُنهَك)، bounce back (يتعافى بسرعة).\nالتعابير الاصطلاحية غير رسمية غالبًا، فنستخدمها في الحديث والرسائل الودية لا في التقارير الرسمية."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Recharge Your Batteries: Well-Being Idioms and Phrasal Verbs”. Let’s learn idioms about health, stress and rest (under the weather, burn the midnight oil, recharge your batteries, on top of the world, keep your cool, let off steam, run out of steam, take it easy); phrasal verbs (wind down, cut down on, work out, burn out, bounce back, calm down, take up, switch off) together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U6-LS3 | Recharge Your Batteries: Well-Being Idioms and Phrasal Verbs","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. mindfulness: the practice of paying calm attention to the present moment. burnout: extreme tiredness caused by working too hard for too long. moderation: not doing too much or too little of something.","on_screen":"mindfulness | burnout | moderation","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Idioms are phrases whose meaning is different from the meanings of the individual words. Feel under the weather = feel a little sick. Burn the midnight oil = study or work late at night. Recharge your batteries = rest to get your energy back. Be on top of the world = feel extremely happy. Keep your cool = stay calm. Let off steam = release energy or anger through activity. Run out of steam = lose energy. Take it easy = relax. Phrasal verbs about well-being: wind down (relax after activity), cut down on (reduce), cut out (stop completely), work out (exercise), burn out (become exhausted from overwork), bounce back (recover quickly), calm down, take up (start a new hobby), switch off (stop thinking about work; turn off a device).","on_screen":"idioms about health, stress and rest (under the weather, burn the midnight oil, recharge your batteries, on top of the world, keep your cool, let off steam, run out of steam, take it easy); phrasal verbs (wind down, cut down on, work out, burn out, bounce back, calm down, take up, switch off)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I'm feeling under the weather, so I'll stay home today. Don't burn the midnight oil before the exam—sleep instead. A weekend in the mountains helped me recharge my batteries.","on_screen":"I'm feeling under the weather, so I'll stay home today. / Don't burn the midnight oil before the exam—sleep instead. / A weekend in the mountains helped me recharge my batteries.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I studied until 2 a.m. – I burned the night oil.” That’s not right. We say: “I burned the midnight oil.” Fixed idiom: the midnight oil.","on_screen":"✗ I studied until 2 a.m. – I burned the night oil.   ✓ I burned the midnight oil.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: If you \"feel under the weather,\" are you outside in the rain? … Think! … No – you feel a little sick. Great job! Now you can say: I can explain \"burn the midnight oil\" and \"recharge your batteries\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can explain \"burn the midnight oil\" and \"recharge your batteries\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: idioms about health, stress and rest (under the weather, burn the midnight oil, recharge your batteries, on top of the world, keep your cool, let off steam, run out of steam, take it easy); phrasal verbs (wind down, cut down on, work out, burn out, bounce back, calm down, take up, switch off).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","التعابير الاصطلاحية معناها مختلف عن معاني كلماتها: under the weather (متوعّك قليلًا)، burn the midnight oil (يسهر للدراسة أو العمل)، recharge your batteries (يستعيد طاقته).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I studied until 2 a.m. – I burned the night oil. — الصحيح: I burned the midnight oil.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أشرح burn the midnight oil وrecharge your batteries."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Ziyad studied until 2 a.m. every night before the exams. He was ___.","options":["under the weather","letting off steam","on top of the world","burning the midnight oil"],"answer":"burning the midnight oil","explanation":"Interpret the idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"I have a slight cold, so I'm feeling a bit ___ today.","options":["over the moon","on top of the world","under the weather","in hot water"],"answer":"under the weather","explanation":"Interpret the idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"My doctor told me to ___ sugar and fizzy drinks.","options":["cut off from","cut up","cut down on","cut in"],"answer":"cut down on","explanation":"Use the right phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب."},{"q":"After a long week, a quiet weekend in Taif helped me ___.","options":["recharge my batteries","run out of steam","keep my cool","burn out"],"answer":"recharge my batteries","explanation":"Interpret the idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"A ___ lifestyle, with many hours of sitting, is bad for your health.","options":["sedentary","hydrated","balanced","mindful"],"answer":"sedentary","explanation":"Well-being vocabulary.","explanation_ar":"مفردات جودة الحياة."},{"q":"Although the team lost its first three matches, it managed to ______, winning the next seven games in a row.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["burn out","bounce back","wind down","cut out"],"answer":"bounce back","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the idiom or phrasal verb to its meaning.","items":[{"q":"keep your cool","options":["relax after a busy time","release energy or anger through activity","stay calm in a difficult situation","become exhausted from working too hard","lose energy and stop","start a new hobby"],"answer":"stay calm in a difficult situation","explanation":"keep your cool → stay calm in a difficult situation. Interpret the idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"let off steam","options":["relax after a busy time","release energy or anger through activity","stay calm in a difficult situation","become exhausted from working too hard","lose energy and stop","start a new hobby"],"answer":"release energy or anger through activity","explanation":"let off steam → release energy or anger through activity. Interpret the idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"run out of steam","options":["relax after a busy time","release energy or anger through activity","stay calm in a difficult situation","become exhausted from working too hard","lose energy and stop","start a new hobby"],"answer":"lose energy and stop","explanation":"run out of steam → lose energy and stop. Interpret the idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"take up","options":["relax after a busy time","release energy or anger through activity","stay calm in a difficult situation","become exhausted from working too hard","lose energy and stop","start a new hobby"],"answer":"start a new hobby","explanation":"take up → start a new hobby. Interpret the idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"wind down","options":["relax after a busy time","release energy or anger through activity","stay calm in a difficult situation","become exhausted from working too hard","lose energy and stop","start a new hobby"],"answer":"relax after a busy time","explanation":"wind down → relax after a busy time. Interpret the idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"burn out","options":["relax after a busy time","release energy or anger through activity","stay calm in a difficult situation","become exhausted from working too hard","lose energy and stop","start a new hobby"],"answer":"become exhausted from working too hard","explanation":"burn out → become exhausted from working too hard. Interpret the idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Talk about your well-being.","items":[{"q":"How do you wind down after a busy day?","options":[],"answer":"I wind down by playing chess with my brother.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses idioms about health, stress and rest (under the weather, burn the midnight oil, recharge your batteries, on top of the world, keep your cool, let off steam, run out of steam, take it easy); phrasal verbs (wind down, cut down on, work out, burn out, bounce back, calm down, take up, switch off) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"When did you last feel on top of the world?","options":[],"answer":"I felt on top of the world when I passed my driving theory test.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses idioms about health, stress and rest (under the weather, burn the midnight oil, recharge your batteries, on top of the world, keep your cool, let off steam, run out of steam, take it easy); phrasal verbs (wind down, cut down on, work out, burn out, bounce back, calm down, take up, switch off) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What would you like to cut down on?","options":[],"answer":"I'd like to cut down on screen time.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses idioms about health, stress and rest (under the weather, burn the midnight oil, recharge your batteries, on top of the world, keep your cool, let off steam, run out of steam, take it easy); phrasal verbs (wind down, cut down on, work out, burn out, bounce back, calm down, take up, switch off) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How do you let off steam?","options":[],"answer":"I let off steam by playing football.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses idioms about health, stress and rest (under the weather, burn the midnight oil, recharge your batteries, on top of the world, keep your cool, let off steam, run out of steam, take it easy); phrasal verbs (wind down, cut down on, work out, burn out, bounce back, calm down, take up, switch off) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A hobby you'd like to take up: ___","options":[],"answer":"I'd like to take up rock climbing.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses idioms about health, stress and rest (under the weather, burn the midnight oil, recharge your batteries, on top of the world, keep your cool, let off steam, run out of steam, take it easy); phrasal verbs (wind down, cut down on, work out, burn out, bounce back, calm down, take up, switch off) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Well-being advice column.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 pieces of advice for a stressed student using 3 idioms or phrasal verbs.","options":[],"answer":"Don't burn the midnight oil. Take it easy on the weekend. Work out a few times a week to let off steam.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses idioms about health, stress and rest (under the weather, burn the midnight oil, recharge your batteries, on top of the world, keep your cool, let off steam, run out of steam, take it easy); phrasal verbs (wind down, cut down on, work out, burn out, bounce back, calm down, take up, switch off) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about how you bounced back from a problem.","options":[],"answer":"I failed my first swimming test. I practiced every day and bounced back two weeks later.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses idioms about health, stress and rest (under the weather, burn the midnight oil, recharge your batteries, on top of the world, keep your cool, let off steam, run out of steam, take it easy); phrasal verbs (wind down, cut down on, work out, burn out, bounce back, calm down, take up, switch off) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Rewrite this informal sentence for a formal report: \"Students should take it easy before exams.\"","options":[],"answer":"Students should rest before examinations.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses idioms about health, stress and rest (under the weather, burn the midnight oil, recharge your batteries, on top of the world, keep your cool, let off steam, run out of steam, take it easy); phrasal verbs (wind down, cut down on, work out, burn out, bounce back, calm down, take up, switch off) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Vocabulary Bingo","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Students write nine words from the list in their grid.","The teacher (or a student caller) reads a definition or Arabic meaning.","Students cross out the matching word.","Three in a row = \"Bingo!\" The winner must read the words and say what each means."],"data":[{"word":"well-being","match":"the state of being healthy, comfortable and happy","arabic":"جودة الحياة / الرفاه"},{"word":"balance","match":"a healthy situation in which different parts of life get the right amount of time","arabic":"توازن"},{"word":"stress","match":"a feeling of worry caused by difficult situations","arabic":"ضغط نفسي / توتر"},{"word":"routine","match":"the usual order in which you do things every day","arabic":"روتين"},{"word":"nutrition","match":"the food you eat and how it affects your health","arabic":"التغذية"},{"word":"hydrated","match":"having enough water in your body","arabic":"رطب / يشرب كفايته من الماء"},{"word":"sedentary","match":"spending a lot of time sitting and not moving much","arabic":"قليل الحركة / خامل"},{"word":"posture","match":"the way you hold your body when you sit or stand","arabic":"وضعية الجسم"},{"word":"mindfulness","match":"the practice of paying calm attention to the present moment","arabic":"اليقظة الذهنية"},{"word":"burnout","match":"extreme tiredness caused by working too hard for too long","arabic":"الإنهاك / الاحتراق الوظيفي"},{"word":"moderation","match":"not doing too much or too little of something","arabic":"الاعتدال"},{"word":"fatigue","match":"a feeling of being extremely tired","arabic":"إرهاق"},{"word":"cope","match":"to deal successfully with a difficult situation","arabic":"يتكيّف / يتعامل مع"},{"word":"unwind","match":"to relax after a period of work or worry","arabic":"يسترخي"},{"word":"overwhelmed","match":"feeling that you have too much to deal with","arabic":"مُثقَل / مغمور"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"When I won the competition, I was ___.","options":["under the weather","burned out","out of steam","on top of the world"],"answer":"on top of the world","explanation":"Interpret the idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"Even when the other team cheated, our captain ___.","options":["let off his cool","lost his cool","kept his cool","blew his cool down"],"answer":"kept his cool","explanation":"Interpret the idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"My uncle ___ every morning at the gym.","options":["works up","works out","works in","works off"],"answer":"works out","explanation":"Use the right phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب."},{"q":"After working twelve hours a day for months, the manager ___.","options":["bounced back","burned out","wound down","took up"],"answer":"burned out","explanation":"Use the right phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب."},{"q":"I've decided to ___ sugar completely—no sweets at all.","options":["cut through","cut up","cut out","cut down on"],"answer":"cut out","explanation":"Use the right phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب."},{"q":"By the last kilometer of the race, he had ___ and could barely walk.","options":["run out of steam","taken it easy","kept his cool","let off steam"],"answer":"run out of steam","explanation":"Interpret the idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"Mindfulness exercises can help you feel less ___ when you have too much to do.","options":["balanced","sedentary","hydrated","overwhelmed"],"answer":"overwhelmed","explanation":"Well-being vocabulary.","explanation_ar":"مفردات جودة الحياة."},{"q":"Remember to stay ___ by drinking water throughout the day.","options":["overwhelmed","moderate","sedentary","hydrated"],"answer":"hydrated","explanation":"Well-being vocabulary.","explanation_ar":"مفردات جودة الحياة."},{"q":"After weeks of preparing for the national exam, Lina felt exhausted, so she spent the holiday reading novels and walking in the park to ______.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["run out of steam","burn the midnight oil","recharge her batteries","lose her cool"],"answer":"recharge her batteries","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."},{"q":"Doctors say that eating sweets is fine in ______; the problem is eating too many of them every day.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["moderation","posture","burnout","fatigue"],"answer":"moderation","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A comic-style poster of idioms: a student studying under a lamp at midnight (burn the midnight oil), a phone-shaped person plugged into a charger (recharge your batteries), a boy on a mountain top cheering (on top of the world), a kettle letting off steam, and a girl wrapped in a blanket with a thermometer (under the weather). Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A comic-style poster of idioms: a student studying under a lamp at midnight (burn the midnight oil), a phone-shaped person plugged into a charger (recharge your batteries), a boy on a mountain top cheering (on top of the world), a kettle letting off steam, and a girl wrapped in a blanket with a thermometer (under the weather)"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 7 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 7 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows mindfulness (the practice of paying calm attention to the present moment); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing mindfulness: the practice of paying calm attention to the present moment"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows burnout (extreme tiredness caused by working too hard for too long); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing burnout: extreme tiredness caused by working too hard for too long"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows moderation (not doing too much or too little of something); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing moderation: not doing too much or too little of something"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows fatigue (a feeling of being extremely tired); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing fatigue: a feeling of being extremely tired"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows cope (to deal successfully with a difficult situation); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing cope: to deal successfully with a difficult situation"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-W06","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows unwind (to relax after a period of work or worry); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing unwind: to relax after a period of work or worry"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-W07","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows overwhelmed (feeling that you have too much to deal with); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing overwhelmed: feeling that you have too much to deal with"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Vocabulary Bingo”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Vocabulary Bingo"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS3-W01","script":"mindfulness. mindfulness. Mindfulness can help you feel calmer before a test.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS3-W02","script":"burnout. burnout. Too much work and too little rest can lead to burnout.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS3-W03","script":"moderation. moderation. Enjoy sweets in moderation.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS3-W04","script":"fatigue. fatigue. Lack of sleep causes fatigue and poor concentration.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS3-W05","script":"cope. cope. She coped well with the pressure of the competition.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS3-W06","script":"unwind. unwind. I unwind by reading before bed.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS3-W07","script":"overwhelmed. overwhelmed. He felt overwhelmed by all his homework.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Recharge Your Batteries: Well-Being Idioms and Phrasal Verbs”. Let’s learn idioms about health, stress and rest (under the weather, burn the midnight oil, recharge your batteries, on top of the world, keep your cool, let off steam, run out of steam, take it easy); phrasal verbs (wind down, cut down on, work out, burn out, bounce back, calm down, take up, switch off) together. Meet some new words. mindfulness: the practice of paying calm attention to the present moment. burnout: extreme tiredness caused by working too hard for too long. moderation: not doing too much or too little of something. Idioms are phrases whose meaning is different from the meanings of the individual words. Feel under the weather = feel a little sick. Burn the midnight oil = study or work late at night. Recharge your batteries = rest to get your energy back. Be on top of the world = feel extremely happy. Keep your cool = stay calm. Let off steam = release energy or anger through activity. Run out of steam = lose energy. Take it easy = relax. Phrasal verbs about well-being: wind down (relax after activity), cut down on (reduce), cut out (stop completely), work out (exercise), burn out (become exhausted from overwork), bounce back (recover quickly), calm down, take up (start a new hobby), switch off (stop thinking about work; turn off a device). Here are some examples. I'm feeling under the weather, so I'll stay home today. Don't burn the midnight oil before the exam—sleep instead. A weekend in the mountains helped me recharge my batteries. Be careful! Some learners say: “I studied until 2 a.m. – I burned the night oil.” That’s not right. We say: “I burned the midnight oil.” Fixed idiom: the midnight oil. Quick check: If you \"feel under the weather,\" are you outside in the rain? … Think! … No – you feel a little sick. Great job! Now you can say: I can explain \"burn the midnight oil\" and \"recharge your batteries\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS4","title":"First, Stretch; Then You Should…: Avoiding Shifts in Voice and Mood","objectives":["Students will be able to recognize and correct inappropriate shifts in voice.","Students will be able to recognize and correct inappropriate shifts in mood, especially in instructions and conditional sentences.","I can fix \"First, stretch your legs, and then you should run slowly.\"","I can fix \"The team trained hard, and the trophy was won by them.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التعرف على التحولات غير المناسبة في البناء (المعلوم والمجهول) وتصحيحها.","سيتمكن الطلاب من التعرف على التحولات غير المناسبة في صيغة الفعل وتصحيحها، خاصة في التعليمات وجمل الشرط.","أستطيع أن أصحّح First, stretch your legs, and then you should run slowly.","أستطيع أن أصحّح The team trained hard, and the trophy was won by them."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"well-being","pos":"noun","ipa":"/wɛlˈbiɪŋ/","definition":"the state of being healthy, comfortable and happy","arabic":"جودة الحياة / الرفاه","example":"Sport and sleep are important for your well-being.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"balance","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbæləns/","definition":"a healthy situation in which different parts of life get the right amount of time","arabic":"توازن","example":"It's hard to find a balance between study and rest.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"stress","pos":"noun","ipa":"/strɛs/","definition":"a feeling of worry caused by difficult situations","arabic":"ضغط نفسي / توتر","example":"Exams can cause a lot of stress.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"routine","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ruˈtin/","definition":"the usual order in which you do things every day","arabic":"روتين","example":"A good morning routine helps me start the day well.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"nutrition","pos":"noun","ipa":"/nuˈtrɪʃən/","definition":"the food you eat and how it affects your health","arabic":"التغذية","example":"Good nutrition gives you energy to learn.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"hydrated","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈhaɪˌdreɪtəd/","definition":"having enough water in your body","arabic":"رطب / يشرب كفايته من الماء","example":"Stay hydrated, especially in summer.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"A shift in voice happens when a sentence changes from active to passive (or the opposite) for no reason, which makes it awkward: (not: The team trained hard, and the trophy was won by them.) → The team trained hard and won the trophy. Keep the same subject and the same voice when you can.\nA shift in mood happens when a sentence mixes moods for no reason. In instructions, keep the imperative: (not: First, stretch your legs, and then you should run slowly.) → First, stretch your legs, and then run slowly. In conditional or subjunctive sentences, keep the pattern: (not: If I were you, I will rest.) → If I were you, I would rest. (not: The doctor recommended that he rest and drinks water.) → … that he rest and drink water.\nShifts are fine when the meaning really changes: Stretch before you run. (imperative + indicative time clause) That's why you must read the whole sentence and ask: Is the change necessary?\nkeep one voice when the subject stays the same\ninstructions → imperative all the way through\nIf I were…, I would… (not will) • recommend that he rest and drink (both base forms)\na shift is OK only when the meaning changes","examples":["Fill your bottle, drink slowly and rest in the shade.","Saad organized his week and finished every task on time.","If I were less busy, I would exercise more.","The nurse recommended that Lina rest and drink plenty of water.","The coach planned the session, and the players followed it carefully.","Sit up straight, relax your shoulders and look at the screen.","The new routine was designed by the counselor and approved by the principal.","It is essential that every student eat breakfast and arrive on time."],"common_errors":["✗ First, stretch your legs, and then you should run slowly. → ✓ First, stretch your legs, and then run slowly. (Instructions → keep the imperative.)","✗ The team trained hard, and the trophy was won by them. → ✓ The team trained hard and won the trophy. (Avoid an unnecessary shift to the passive.)","✗ If I were you, I will take a break. → ✓ If I were you, I would take a break. (Keep the conditional mood.)","✗ The doctor recommended that he rest and drinks water. → ✓ The doctor recommended that he rest and drink water. (Keep both verbs in the subjunctive.)"],"arabic":"التحوّل في البناء: الانتقال من المعلوم إلى المجهول دون سبب يجعل الجملة ركيكة: The team trained hard and won the trophy (وليس and the trophy was won by them).\nالتحوّل في الصيغة: في التعليمات نلتزم بصيغة الأمر حتى النهاية: stretch… then run (وليس then you should run).\nفي جمل الشرط والـ subjunctive نحافظ على النمط: If I were you, I would…، وrecommended that he rest and drink.\nالتحوّل مقبول فقط عندما يتغيّر المعنى فعلًا. وهذه من مهارات SAT في Form, Structure, and Sense."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “First, Stretch; Then You Should…: Avoiding Shifts in Voice and Mood”. Let’s learn inappropriate shifts in verb voice (active ↔ passive) and verb mood (imperative ↔ indicative, conditional ↔ indicative, subjunctive ↔ indicative) within a sentence or a set of instructions together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U6-LS4 | First, Stretch; Then You Should…: Avoiding Shifts in Voice and Mood","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"A shift in voice happens when a sentence changes from active to passive (or the opposite) for no reason, which makes it awkward: (not: The team trained hard, and the trophy was won by them.) → The team trained hard and won the trophy. Keep the same subject and the same voice when you can.","on_screen":"inappropriate shifts in verb voice (active ↔ passive) and verb mood (imperative ↔ indicative, conditional ↔ indicative, subjunctive ↔ indicative) within a sentence or a set of instructions","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"A shift in voice happens when a sentence changes from active to passive (or the opposite) for no reason, which makes it awkward: (not: The team trained hard, and the trophy was won by them.) → The team trained hard and won the trophy. Keep the same subject and the same voice when you can. A shift in mood happens when a sentence mixes moods for no reason. In instructions, keep the imperative: (not: First, stretch your legs, and then you should run slowly.) → First, stretch your legs, and then run slowly. In conditional or subjunctive sentences, keep the pattern: (not: If I were you, I will rest.) → If I were you, I would rest. (not: The doctor recommended that he rest and drinks water.) → … that he rest and drink water.","on_screen":"keep one voice when the subject stays the same • instructions → imperative all the way through • If I were…, I would… (not will) • recommend that he rest and drink (both base forms)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Fill your bottle, drink slowly and rest in the shade. Saad organized his week and finished every task on time. If I were less busy, I would exercise more.","on_screen":"Fill your bottle, drink slowly and rest in the shade. / Saad organized his week and finished every task on time. / If I were less busy, I would exercise more.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “First, stretch your legs, and then you should run slowly.” That’s not right. We say: “First, stretch your legs, and then run slowly.” Instructions → keep the imperative.","on_screen":"✗ First, stretch your legs, and then you should run slowly.   ✓ First, stretch your legs, and then run slowly.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"Stretch, and then you should run.\" What's wrong? … Think! … It shifts from imperative to indicative. Great job! Now you can say: I can fix \"First, stretch your legs, and then you should run slowly.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can fix \"First, stretch your legs, and then you should run slowly.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: inappropriate shifts in verb voice (active ↔ passive) and verb mood (imperative ↔ indicative, conditional ↔ indicative, subjunctive ↔ indicative) within a sentence or a set of instructions.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","التحوّل في البناء: الانتقال من المعلوم إلى المجهول دون سبب يجعل الجملة ركيكة: The team trained hard and won the trophy (وليس and the trophy was won by them).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: First, stretch your legs, and then you should run slowly. — الصحيح: First, stretch your legs, and then run slowly.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أصحّح First, stretch your legs, and then you should run slowly."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Five Steps to a Better Night's Sleep (editing passage)","body":"First, put your phone in another room. Then you should dim the lights an hour before bed. Read a book or you could listen to calm sounds. Keep your bedroom cool, and the curtains should be closed. Coffee should be avoided in the evening. Finally, you go to bed at the same time every night.","word_count":55,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the best sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["First, you stretch your legs, and then run slowly.","First, stretch your legs, and then running slowly.","First, stretch your legs, and then you should run slowly.","First, stretch your legs, and then run slowly."],"answer":"First, stretch your legs, and then run slowly.","explanation":"Instructions → keep the imperative.","explanation_ar":"التعليمات بصيغة الأمر."},{"q":"","options":["Hard training was done, and the team won the trophy.","The team trained hard, and the trophy was won by them.","The team trained hard and won the trophy.","The team was trained hard and won the trophy by them."],"answer":"The team trained hard and won the trophy.","explanation":"Avoid an unnecessary shift in voice.","explanation_ar":"التحوّل في البناء."},{"q":"","options":["If I were you, I take a break.","If I were you, I would take a break.","If I was you, I take a break.","If I were you, I will take a break."],"answer":"If I were you, I would take a break.","explanation":"Keep the conditional / subjunctive pattern.","explanation_ar":"نمط الشرط."},{"q":"","options":["The doctor recommended that he rests and drink water.","The doctor recommended that he resting and drink water.","The doctor recommended that he rest and drink water.","The doctor recommended that he rest and drinks water."],"answer":"The doctor recommended that he rest and drink water.","explanation":"Avoid an unnecessary shift in mood.","explanation_ar":"التحوّل في الصيغة."},{"q":"Which sentence has a correct, necessary shift?","options":["Stretch before you run.","You stretch first, and then run.","Stretch first, and then you should run.","Stretch, and then you are running."],"answer":"Stretch before you run.","explanation":"A shift is correct when the meaning changes.","explanation_ar":"التحوّل الصحيح."},{"q":"To prepare for the race, the runners followed a strict plan: they slept eight hours a night, ate balanced meals and ______ every morning at six.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["were trained by coaches","trained","had been trained","training"],"answer":"trained","explanation":"Avoid an unnecessary shift in voice.","explanation_ar":"التحوّل في البناء."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite the instructions in the imperative.","items":[{"q":"Sit up straight, and you should relax your shoulders.  (imperative)","options":[],"answer":"Sit up straight, and relax your shoulders.","explanation":"Instructions → keep the imperative.","explanation_ar":"التعليمات بصيغة الأمر."},{"q":"Fill your bottle, and you can drink it slowly.  (imperative)","options":[],"answer":"Fill your bottle, and drink it slowly.","explanation":"Instructions → keep the imperative.","explanation_ar":"التعليمات بصيغة الأمر."},{"q":"First, you take a deep breath, and then count to five.  (imperative)","options":[],"answer":"First, take a deep breath, and then count to five.","explanation":"Instructions → keep the imperative.","explanation_ar":"التعليمات بصيغة الأمر."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS4-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"Lina planned her week, and every task was finished by her on time.","options":[],"answer":"Lina planned her week, and she finished every task on time.","explanation":"every task was finished by her → she finished every task. Avoid an unnecessary shift in voice.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: every task was finished by her → she finished every task. التحوّل في البناء."},{"q":"If he were less tired, he will enjoy the trip more.","options":[],"answer":"If he were less tired, he would enjoy the trip more.","explanation":"will → would. Keep the conditional / subjunctive pattern.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: will → would. نمط الشرط."},{"q":"It is essential that every student eat breakfast and arrives on time.","options":[],"answer":"It is essential that every student eat breakfast and arrive on time.","explanation":"arrives → arrive. Avoid an unnecessary shift in mood.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: arrives → arrive. التحوّل في الصيغة."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the instructions.","items":[{"q":"Then you should dim the lights an hour before bed.","options":[],"answer":"Then dim the lights an hour before bed.","explanation":"you should dim → dim. Avoid an unnecessary shift in voice.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: you should dim → dim. التحوّل في البناء."},{"q":"Read a book or you could listen to calm sounds.","options":[],"answer":"Read a book or listen to calm sounds.","explanation":"you could listen → listen. Avoid an unnecessary shift in voice.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: you could listen → listen. التحوّل في البناء."},{"q":"Keep your bedroom cool, and the curtains should be closed. Avoid coffee in the evening.","options":[],"answer":"Keep your bedroom cool, and close the curtains. Avoid coffee in the evening.","explanation":"the curtains should be closed → close the curtains. Avoid an unnecessary shift in voice.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: the curtains should be closed → close the curtains. التحوّل في البناء."},{"q":"Keep your bedroom cool, and close the curtains. Coffee should be avoided in the evening.","options":[],"answer":"Keep your bedroom cool, and close the curtains. Avoid coffee in the evening.","explanation":"Coffee should be avoided → Avoid coffee. Avoid an unnecessary shift in voice.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Coffee should be avoided → Avoid coffee. التحوّل في البناء."},{"q":"Finally, you go to bed at the same time every night.","options":[],"answer":"Finally, go to bed at the same time every night.","explanation":"you go → go. Avoid an unnecessary shift in voice.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: you go → go. التحوّل في البناء."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write consistent sentences.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 imperative steps for a short stretching routine.","options":[],"answer":"Stand up straight. Raise your arms above your head. Hold for ten seconds and breathe slowly.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inappropriate shifts in verb voice (active ↔ passive) and verb mood (imperative ↔ indicative, conditional ↔ indicative, subjunctive ↔ indicative) within a sentence or a set of instructions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with two active verbs and the same subject.","options":[],"answer":"Faisal cooked dinner and washed the dishes.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inappropriate shifts in verb voice (active ↔ passive) and verb mood (imperative ↔ indicative, conditional ↔ indicative, subjunctive ↔ indicative) within a sentence or a set of instructions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one subjunctive sentence with two base-form verbs.","options":[],"answer":"The coach insists that every player warm up and cool down properly.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inappropriate shifts in verb voice (active ↔ passive) and verb mood (imperative ↔ indicative, conditional ↔ indicative, subjunctive ↔ indicative) within a sentence or a set of instructions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Letter Ladder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The leader chooses a word from the list and draws one blank line per letter.","Teams take turns guessing letters. Correct letters are written on the lines.","Each wrong guess removes one rung of the ladder (start with 6 rungs).","The team that completes the word scores 2 points and uses it in a sentence."],"data":[{"word":"well-being","clue":"the state of being healthy, comfortable and happy"},{"word":"nutrition","clue":"the food you eat and how it affects your health"},{"word":"posture","clue":"the way you hold your body when you sit or stand"},{"word":"mindfulness","clue":"the practice of paying calm attention to the present moment"},{"word":"fatigue","clue":"a feeling of being extremely tired"},{"word":"overwhelmed","clue":"feeling that you have too much to deal with"},{"word":"balance","clue":"a healthy situation in which different parts of life get the right amount of time"},{"word":"stress","clue":"a feeling of worry caused by difficult situations"},{"word":"routine","clue":"the usual order in which you do things every day"},{"word":"hydrated","clue":"having enough water in your body"},{"word":"sedentary","clue":"spending a lot of time sitting and not moving much"},{"word":"burnout","clue":"extreme tiredness caused by working too hard for too long"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["Breathe in slowly, hold your breath and breathe out.","Breathing in slowly, hold your breath and breathe out.","Breathe in slowly, you hold your breath and breathe out.","Breathe in slowly, hold your breath and you should breathe out."],"answer":"Breathe in slowly, hold your breath and breathe out.","explanation":"Instructions → keep the imperative.","explanation_ar":"التعليمات بصيغة الأمر."},{"q":"","options":["The volunteers cleaned the park, and new trees were planted by them.","The volunteers cleaned the park and planted new trees.","The park was cleaned by the volunteers, and they planted new trees by them.","The volunteers cleaned the park, and trees planting were done."],"answer":"The volunteers cleaned the park and planted new trees.","explanation":"Avoid an unnecessary shift in voice.","explanation_ar":"التحوّل في البناء."},{"q":"","options":["If she was more organized, she feels less stressed.","If she were more organized, she feels less stressed.","If she were more organized, she would feel less stressed.","If she were more organized, she will feel less stressed."],"answer":"If she were more organized, she would feel less stressed.","explanation":"Keep the conditional / subjunctive pattern.","explanation_ar":"نمط الشرط."},{"q":"","options":["The nurse suggested that Omar sleep more and eats less sugar.","The nurse suggested that Omar sleep more and eat less sugar.","The nurse suggested that Omar sleeping more and eating less sugar.","The nurse suggested that Omar sleeps more and eat less sugar."],"answer":"The nurse suggested that Omar sleep more and eat less sugar.","explanation":"Avoid an unnecessary shift in mood.","explanation_ar":"التحوّل في الصيغة."},{"q":"Which sentence has an unnecessary shift in mood?","options":["You should turn off the TV and read a book.","Turn off the TV and read a book.","If you turn off the TV, you can read a book.","Turn off the TV, and you should read a book."],"answer":"Turn off the TV, and you should read a book.","explanation":"Avoid an unnecessary shift in mood.","explanation_ar":"التحوّل في الصيغة."},{"q":"Which sentence has an unnecessary shift in voice?","options":["Adam wrote and submitted the essay on Sunday.","Adam wrote the essay and submitted it on Sunday.","The essay was written and submitted on Sunday.","Adam wrote the essay, and it was submitted by him on Sunday."],"answer":"Adam wrote the essay, and it was submitted by him on Sunday.","explanation":"Avoid an unnecessary shift in voice.","explanation_ar":"التحوّل في البناء."},{"q":"Which sentence shifts correctly because the meaning changes?","options":["Rest now, and you should drink water.","If I were you, I will rest now.","Rest now, because you will need energy tomorrow.","Rest now, and water should be drunk."],"answer":"Rest now, because you will need energy tomorrow.","explanation":"A shift is correct when the meaning changes.","explanation_ar":"التحوّل الصحيح."},{"q":"Mix the flour and the dates, ______ the mixture into small balls, and bake them for fifteen minutes.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["roll","you should roll","rolling","the mixture is rolled"],"answer":"roll","explanation":"Instructions → keep the imperative.","explanation_ar":"التعليمات بصيغة الأمر."},{"q":"The research team collected data from five hundred students and ______ that those who slept more than eight hours scored higher on memory tests.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["it was found by them","found","was found","finding"],"answer":"found","explanation":"Avoid an unnecessary shift in voice.","explanation_ar":"التحوّل في البناء."},{"q":"It is important that each participant complete the survey and ______ it by Friday.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["returned","is returning","return","returns"],"answer":"return","explanation":"Avoid an unnecessary shift in mood.","explanation_ar":"التحوّل في الصيغة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Balance and Well-Being” that shows inappropriate shifts in verb voice (active ↔ passive) and verb mood (imperative ↔ indicative, conditional ↔ indicative, subjunctive ↔ indicative) within a sentence or a set of instructions in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Balance and Well-Being” that shows inappropriate shifts in verb voice (active ↔ passive) and verb mood (imperative ↔ indicative, conditional ↔ indicative, subjunctive ↔ indicative) within a sentence or a set of instructions in action"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Letter Ladder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Letter Ladder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “First, Stretch; Then You Should…: Avoiding Shifts in Voice and Mood”. Let’s learn inappropriate shifts in verb voice (active ↔ passive) and verb mood (imperative ↔ indicative, conditional ↔ indicative, subjunctive ↔ indicative) within a sentence or a set of instructions together. A shift in voice happens when a sentence changes from active to passive (or the opposite) for no reason, which makes it awkward: (not: The team trained hard, and the trophy was won by them.) → The team trained hard and won the trophy. Keep the same subject and the same voice when you can. A shift in voice happens when a sentence changes from active to passive (or the opposite) for no reason, which makes it awkward: (not: The team trained hard, and the trophy was won by them.) → The team trained hard and won the trophy. Keep the same subject and the same voice when you can. A shift in mood happens when a sentence mixes moods for no reason. In instructions, keep the imperative: (not: First, stretch your legs, and then you should run slowly.) → First, stretch your legs, and then run slowly. In conditional or subjunctive sentences, keep the pattern: (not: If I were you, I will rest.) → If I were you, I would rest. (not: The doctor recommended that he rest and drinks water.) → … that he rest and drink water. Here are some examples. Fill your bottle, drink slowly and rest in the shade. Saad organized his week and finished every task on time. If I were less busy, I would exercise more. Be careful! Some learners say: “First, stretch your legs, and then you should run slowly.” That’s not right. We say: “First, stretch your legs, and then run slowly.” Instructions → keep the imperative. Quick check: \"Stretch, and then you should run.\" What's wrong? … Think! … It shifts from imperative to indicative. Great job! Now you can say: I can fix \"First, stretch your legs, and then you should run slowly.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS5","title":"A Letter of Advice: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to give spoken advice about well-being in different moods.","Students will be able to write a letter of advice with imperatives, the subjunctive, idioms and consistent voice and mood, and answer SAT-style transition and synthesis items.","I can give a friend advice about stress.","I can write a friendly letter of advice."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تقديم نصائح شفهية عن جودة الحياة بصيغ مختلفة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة رسالة نصح بصيغة الأمر والـ subjunctive والتعابير الاصطلاحية مع اتساق البناء والصيغة، والإجابة عن أسئلة الروابط والتركيب بنمط SAT.","أستطيع أن أنصح صديقًا بشأن التوتر.","أستطيع أن أكتب رسالة نصح ودية."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"well-being","pos":"noun","ipa":"/wɛlˈbiɪŋ/","definition":"the state of being healthy, comfortable and happy","arabic":"جودة الحياة / الرفاه","example":"Sport and sleep are important for your well-being.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"balance","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbæləns/","definition":"a healthy situation in which different parts of life get the right amount of time","arabic":"توازن","example":"It's hard to find a balance between study and rest.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"stress","pos":"noun","ipa":"/strɛs/","definition":"a feeling of worry caused by difficult situations","arabic":"ضغط نفسي / توتر","example":"Exams can cause a lot of stress.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"routine","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ruˈtin/","definition":"the usual order in which you do things every day","arabic":"روتين","example":"A good morning routine helps me start the day well.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"nutrition","pos":"noun","ipa":"/nuˈtrɪʃən/","definition":"the food you eat and how it affects your health","arabic":"التغذية","example":"Good nutrition gives you energy to learn.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"hydrated","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈhaɪˌdreɪtəd/","definition":"having enough water in your body","arabic":"رطب / يشرب كفايته من الماء","example":"Stay hydrated, especially in summer.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sedentary","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈsɛdənˌtɛri/","definition":"spending a lot of time sitting and not moving much","arabic":"قليل الحركة / خامل","example":"A sedentary lifestyle can lead to health problems.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"posture","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɑstʃɚ/","definition":"the way you hold your body when you sit or stand","arabic":"وضعية الجسم","example":"Sit up straight; good posture protects your back.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"mindfulness","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmaɪndfəlnəs/","definition":"the practice of paying calm attention to the present moment","arabic":"اليقظة الذهنية","example":"Mindfulness can help you feel calmer before a test.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"burnout","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbɝˌnaʊt/","definition":"extreme tiredness caused by working too hard for too long","arabic":"الإنهاك / الاحتراق الوظيفي","example":"Too much work and too little rest can lead to burnout.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"moderation","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌmɑdɚˈeɪʃən/","definition":"not doing too much or too little of something","arabic":"الاعتدال","example":"Enjoy sweets in moderation.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"fatigue","pos":"noun","ipa":"/fəˈtiɡ/","definition":"a feeling of being extremely tired","arabic":"إرهاق","example":"Lack of sleep causes fatigue and poor concentration.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"cope","pos":"verb","ipa":"/koʊp/","definition":"to deal successfully with a difficult situation","arabic":"يتكيّف / يتعامل مع","example":"She coped well with the pressure of the competition.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"unwind","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ənˈwaɪnd/","definition":"to relax after a period of work or worry","arabic":"يسترخي","example":"I unwind by reading before bed.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"overwhelmed","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌoʊvɚˈwɛlmd/","definition":"feeling that you have too much to deal with","arabic":"مُثقَل / مغمور","example":"He felt overwhelmed by all his homework.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 6: the five verb moods, the subjunctive after verbs and adjectives, well-being idioms and phrasal verbs, and consistent voice and mood.\nA friendly letter of advice shows sympathy, gives clear advice (imperatives, If I were you…), adds expert recommendations (My doctor recommended that I…) and ends positively. Idioms make it warm and natural. In SAT-style questions, choose transitions that show the logical link and sentences that use notes to meet a specific goal.\n✔ imperative: Take… / Don't…\n✔ If I were you, I would…\n✔ recommend that I drink • It is important that you be…\n✔ idioms: on top of the world, burn the midnight oil, let off steam","examples":["Get some fresh air every afternoon.","Don't compare yourself to others.","If I were you, I would join the swimming club to let off steam.","My coach insists that every player rest one day a week.","It is essential that you eat breakfast before the exam.","You'll bounce back quickly, I'm sure.","Take it easy this weekend and recharge your batteries.","I hope you feel better soon."],"common_errors":["✗ If I was you, I will sleep more. → ✓ If I were you, I would sleep more. (Subjunctive were + conditional would.)","✗ My doctor recommended that I drank more water. → ✓ My doctor recommended that I drink more water. (Subjunctive → base form.)","✗ Take a break, and you should go for a walk. → ✓ Take a break, and go for a walk. (Keep the imperative.)"],"arabic":"نراجع صيغ الفعل الخمس والـ subjunctive والتعابير الاصطلاحية والأفعال المركبة واتساق البناء والصيغة.\nرسالة النصح الودية تُظهر التعاطف، وتقدّم نصائح واضحة، وتذكر توصيات الخبراء، وتنتهي بشكل إيجابي.\nالتعابير الاصطلاحية تجعل الرسالة دافئة وطبيعية."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Letter of Advice: Language in Use”. Let’s learn verb moods and the subjunctive, well-being idioms and phrasal verbs, consistency in voice and mood; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U6-LS5 | A Letter of Advice: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Well-being hotline: in pairs, one student calls a \"well-being hotline\" with a problem (exam stress, too much screen time, no time for hobbies). The other gives advice using one imperative, one \"If I were you…\", one subjunctive recommendation and one idiom. Then swap roles.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 6: the five verb moods, the subjunctive after verbs and adjectives, well-being idioms and phrasal verbs, and consistent voice and mood. A friendly letter of advice shows sympathy, gives clear advice (imperatives, If I were you…), adds expert recommendations (My doctor recommended that I…) and ends positively. Idioms make it warm and natural. In SAT-style questions, choose transitions that show the logical link and sentences that use notes to meet a specific goal.","on_screen":"✔ imperative: Take… / Don't… • ✔ If I were you, I would… • ✔ recommend that I drink • It is important that you be…","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Get some fresh air every afternoon. Don't compare yourself to others. If I were you, I would join the swimming club to let off steam.","on_screen":"Get some fresh air every afternoon. / Don't compare yourself to others. / If I were you, I would join the swimming club to let off steam.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “If I was you, I will sleep more.” That’s not right. We say: “If I were you, I would sleep more.” Subjunctive were + conditional would.","on_screen":"✗ If I was you, I will sleep more.   ✓ If I were you, I would sleep more.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “My doctor recommended that I drank more water.”? … Think! … It should be “My doctor recommended that I drink more water.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can give a friend advice about stress.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can give a friend advice about stress.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: verb moods and the subjunctive, well-being idioms and phrasal verbs, consistency in voice and mood; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع صيغ الفعل الخمس والـ subjunctive والتعابير الاصطلاحية والأفعال المركبة واتساق البناء والصيغة.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: If I was you, I will sleep more. — الصحيح: If I were you, I would sleep more.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أنصح صديقًا بشأن التوتر."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"A Letter to Ziyad – Faisal","body":"Dear Ziyad,\nI'm sorry to hear that you've been feeling stressed out about the exams.\nIf I were you, I would make a simple study timetable and stick to it.\nFirst, take a short break every hour, and go for a walk if you can.\nMy doctor once recommended that I drink more water and that I not study late at night, and it really helped.\nIt is important that you be kind to yourself; nobody is perfect.\nDon't burn the midnight oil before the exam—get a good night's sleep instead.\nI hope you'll be on top of the world when the results come out!\nYour friend, Faisal","word_count":108,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Faisal's letter. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Ziyad has been feeling stressed about the exams.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Letter to Ziyad – Faisal”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Faisal advises Ziyad to study late every night.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “A Letter to Ziyad – Faisal”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Faisal suggests taking a short break every hour.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Letter to Ziyad – Faisal”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Faisal's doctor recommended that he drink more water.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Letter to Ziyad – Faisal”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Faisal says that everyone is perfect.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “A Letter to Ziyad – Faisal”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Faisal hopes Ziyad will feel very happy when the results come out.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Letter to Ziyad – Faisal”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"If I ___ you, I would make a study timetable.","options":["were","am","will be","was being"],"answer":"were","explanation":"Verb mood or subjunctive.","explanation_ar":"صيغة الفعل."},{"q":"My doctor recommended that I ___ more water.","options":["drink","drank","drinks","drinking"],"answer":"drink","explanation":"Verb mood or subjunctive.","explanation_ar":"صيغة الفعل."},{"q":"It is important that you ___ kind to yourself.","options":["are","were","be","being"],"answer":"be","explanation":"Verb mood or subjunctive.","explanation_ar":"صيغة الفعل."},{"q":"\"Don't burn the midnight oil\" means don't ___.","options":["cook at midnight","waste electricity","go out at night","study late at night"],"answer":"study late at night","explanation":"Well-being idiom or phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"","options":["Take a short break every hour, and you should go for a walk.","Take a short break every hour, and go for a walk.","Take a short break every hour, and a walk should be taken.","Taking a short break every hour, and go for a walk."],"answer":"Take a short break every hour, and go for a walk.","explanation":"Consistent voice and mood.","explanation_ar":"الاتساق."},{"q":"Ziyad had been studying for ten hours a day for weeks. ______ he felt exhausted and could not concentrate.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["For example,","As a result,","In contrast,","However,"],"answer":"As a result,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Well-being hotline: write your notes.","items":[{"q":"The caller's problem: ___","options":[],"answer":"He spends six hours a day playing video games and feels tired.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb moods and the subjunctive, well-being idioms and phrasal verbs, consistency in voice and mood; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Advice with an imperative: ___","options":[],"answer":"Set a timer and stop after one hour.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb moods and the subjunctive, well-being idioms and phrasal verbs, consistency in voice and mood; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Advice with \"If I were you…\": ___","options":[],"answer":"If I were you, I'd take up a sport.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb moods and the subjunctive, well-being idioms and phrasal verbs, consistency in voice and mood; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A subjunctive recommendation: ___","options":[],"answer":"My cousin's doctor recommends that teenagers spend at least an hour outdoors.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb moods and the subjunctive, well-being idioms and phrasal verbs, consistency in voice and mood; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"An idiom or phrasal verb to finish: ___","options":[],"answer":"You'll bounce back in no time!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb moods and the subjunctive, well-being idioms and phrasal verbs, consistency in voice and mood; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your letter of advice.","items":[{"q":"Plan: friend's name, problem, sympathy, three pieces of advice, an expert recommendation, a positive ending.","options":[],"answer":"Saad; feels overwhelmed by homework and training; sorry to hear; make a weekly plan, say no to some activities, sleep earlier; coach recommends one rest day; you'll be on top of the world soon","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb moods and the subjunctive, well-being idioms and phrasal verbs, consistency in voice and mood; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your letter of advice in 8–9 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Dear Saad, I'm sorry to hear that you've been feeling overwhelmed. If I were you, I would make a weekly plan for homework and training. Don't say yes to every activity; choose the ones you love. Our coach always recommends that players rest one day a week, and it really works. It is important that you get at least eight hours of sleep. On Fridays, switch off your phone and recharge your batteries. Remember that everyone runs out of steam sometimes. I'm sure you'll be on top of the world again soon! Your friend, Omar","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb moods and the subjunctive, well-being idioms and phrasal verbs, consistency in voice and mood; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: subjunctive base forms? If I were… I would…? imperatives consistent? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"recommends that players rests\" to \"recommends that players rest\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb moods and the subjunctive, well-being idioms and phrasal verbs, consistency in voice and mood; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Treasure Hunt Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams move to a station every 90 seconds.","At each station, write one correct sentence with the cue word and verb moods and the subjunctive, well-being idioms and phrasal verbs, consistency in voice and mood; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review).","Teams collect a \"treasure letter\" for each correct sentence.","Unscramble the letters at the end to reveal the secret word."],"data":[{"cue":"well-being","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"balance","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"stress","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"routine","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"nutrition","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"hydrated","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"sedentary","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"posture","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"mindfulness","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"burnout","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"moderation","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"fatigue","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"cope","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"unwind","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"overwhelmed","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"If I ___ less busy, I would join the art club.","options":["am","were","been","will be"],"answer":"were","explanation":"Verb mood or subjunctive.","explanation_ar":"صيغة الفعل."},{"q":"The coach insists that every player ___ a rest day each week.","options":["take","takes","took","taking"],"answer":"take","explanation":"Verb mood or subjunctive.","explanation_ar":"صيغة الفعل."},{"q":"\"___ yourself to others,\" the counselor said.","options":["No comparing you","You don't compare","Don't compare","Not compare"],"answer":"Don't compare","explanation":"Verb mood or subjunctive.","explanation_ar":"صيغة الفعل."},{"q":"After a long week, I like to ___ by reading a novel.","options":["cut out","wind down","burn out","run out"],"answer":"wind down","explanation":"Well-being idiom or phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"","options":["Turn off your phone and enjoy dinner with your family.","Turn off your phone, and dinner should be enjoyed.","Turning off your phone and enjoy dinner with your family.","Turn off your phone, and you should enjoy dinner with your family."],"answer":"Turn off your phone and enjoy dinner with your family.","explanation":"Consistent voice and mood.","explanation_ar":"الاتساق."},{"q":"Many students believe that studying all night improves their results. ______ research shows that sleep helps the brain store new information.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Therefore,","Similarly,","For example,","However,"],"answer":"However,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"Short walks during the school day have many benefits. ______ they improve concentration, reduce stress and help students sleep better at night.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["However,","Nevertheless,","For example,","Instead,"],"answer":"For example,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Teenagers need eight to ten hours of sleep a night.\n• Many teenagers sleep less than seven hours.\n• Screens before bed can make it harder to fall asleep.\n• Sleep helps the brain store memories.\n\nThe student wants to suggest a solution to teenagers' lack of sleep. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Because screens before bed make it harder to fall asleep, teenagers who switch off their devices earlier may get closer to the eight to ten hours of sleep they need.","Many teenagers sleep less than seven hours a night.","Teenagers need eight to ten hours of sleep a night.","Sleep helps the brain store memories."],"answer":"Because screens before bed make it harder to fall asleep, teenagers who switch off their devices earlier may get closer to the eight to ten hours of sleep they need.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Mindfulness means paying calm attention to the present moment.\n• Some schools offer short mindfulness sessions.\n• Studies suggest that mindfulness can reduce stress.\n• Sessions often last only five to ten minutes.\n\nThe student wants to show that mindfulness is easy to fit into a school day. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Mindfulness means paying calm attention to the present moment.","Some schools offer mindfulness sessions.","Studies suggest that mindfulness can reduce stress.","Because mindfulness sessions often last only five to ten minutes, schools can easily include them in a busy day."],"answer":"Because mindfulness sessions often last only five to ten minutes, schools can easily include them in a busy day.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a letter of advice:","options":["If I was you, I will take up swimming; it's a great way to let out steam.","If I were you, I take up swimming, it's a great way to let off steam.","If I were you, swimming would be taken up to let off steam.","If I were you, I would take up swimming; it's a great way to let off steam."],"answer":"If I were you, I would take up swimming; it's a great way to let off steam.","explanation":"Verb mood or subjunctive.","explanation_ar":"صيغة الفعل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Faisal writing a letter at his desk, with a photo of his friend Ziyad looking tired in front of a pile of books; a wall calendar with \"Exams\" circled and a small plant and water bottle on the desk. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Faisal writing a letter at his desk, with a photo of his friend Ziyad looking tired in front of a pile of books; a wall calendar with \"Exams\" circled and a small plant and water bottle on the desk"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Balance and Well-Being”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Balance and Well-Being”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L08-U6-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Treasure Hunt Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Treasure Hunt Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS5-T1","script":"Dear Ziyad, I'm sorry to hear that you've been feeling stressed out about the exams. If I were you, I would make a simple study timetable and stick to it. First, take a short break every hour, and go for a walk if you can. My doctor once recommended that I drink more water and that I not study late at night, and it really helped. It is important that you be kind to yourself; nobody is perfect. Don't burn the midnight oil before the exam—get a good night's sleep instead. I hope you'll be on top of the world when the results come out! Your friend, Faisal","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U6-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Letter of Advice: Language in Use”. Let’s learn verb moods and the subjunctive, well-being idioms and phrasal verbs, consistency in voice and mood; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Well-being hotline: in pairs, one student calls a \"well-being hotline\" with a problem (exam stress, too much screen time, no time for hobbies). The other gives advice using one imperative, one \"If I were you…\", one subjunctive recommendation and one idiom. Then swap roles. Today you use all of Unit 6: the five verb moods, the subjunctive after verbs and adjectives, well-being idioms and phrasal verbs, and consistent voice and mood. A friendly letter of advice shows sympathy, gives clear advice (imperatives, If I were you…), adds expert recommendations (My doctor recommended that I…) and ends positively. Idioms make it warm and natural. In SAT-style questions, choose transitions that show the logical link and sentences that use notes to meet a specific goal. Here are some examples. Get some fresh air every afternoon. Don't compare yourself to others. If I were you, I would join the swimming club to let off steam. Be careful! Some learners say: “If I was you, I will sleep more.” That’s not right. We say: “If I were you, I would sleep more.” Subjunctive were + conditional would. Quick check: what is wrong with “My doctor recommended that I drank more water.”? … Think! … It should be “My doctor recommended that I drink more water.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can give a friend advice about stress.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"If I ___ the coach, I would give the team a day off.","options":["were","am","will be","was being"],"answer":"were","explanation":"Subjunctive were – unreal situation.","explanation_ar":"were للمواقف غير الحقيقية."},{"q":"The doctor recommended that my grandfather ___ every day.","options":["is walking","walked","walks","walk"],"answer":"walk","explanation":"Subjunctive base form after recommend / essential that.","explanation_ar":"المصدر بعد recommend that."},{"q":"\"___ water before you feel thirsty,\" the trainer said.","options":["Drink","To drink","Drinks","You drink"],"answer":"Drink","explanation":"Imperative – a command or advice.","explanation_ar":"الأمر."},{"q":"Which sentence describes an imaginary situation with \"would\"?","options":["Do you sleep with your phone in the room?","Sleep without your phone in the room.","I would sleep better without my phone in the room.","I sleep better without my phone in the room."],"answer":"I would sleep better without my phone in the room.","explanation":"Conditional – would / could / might.","explanation_ar":"الشرط."},{"q":"It is essential that the patient ___ the medicine at the same time every day.","options":["takes","took","taking","take"],"answer":"take","explanation":"It is + adjective + that + base form.","explanation_ar":"الصفة + that + المصدر."},{"q":"The team doctor insisted that the injured player ______ in the final, even though he felt ready to play.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["not competing","does not compete","not compete","did not compete"],"answer":"not compete","explanation":"Negative subjunctive: not + base form.","explanation_ar":"النفي."},{"q":"It is vital that all sports equipment ___ checked before use.","options":["be","being","is","was"],"answer":"be","explanation":"Passive subjunctive: be + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المجهول."},{"q":"","options":["The counselor suggested to keep a gratitude journal.","The counselor suggested us to keep a gratitude journal.","The counselor suggested keeping a gratitude journal.","The counselor suggested that we keeping a gratitude journal."],"answer":"The counselor suggested keeping a gratitude journal.","explanation":"suggest + -ing / advise + person + to.","explanation_ar":"البدائل."},{"q":"My little sister acts as if she ___ the oldest child in the family.","options":["been","is being","were","will be"],"answer":"were","explanation":"Subjunctive were – unreal situation.","explanation_ar":"were للمواقف غير الحقيقية."},{"q":"Hamad stayed up until 3 a.m. studying. He was ___.","options":["burning the midnight oil","under the weather","letting off steam","on top of the world"],"answer":"burning the midnight oil","explanation":"Interpret the idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"I've started going to the gym, where I ___ three times a week.","options":["work in","work off","work up","work out"],"answer":"work out","explanation":"Use the right phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب."},{"q":"After the exams, I went to the beach to ___ and relax.","options":["run out of steam","recharge my batteries","burn out","lose my cool"],"answer":"recharge my batteries","explanation":"Interpret the idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"Sitting at a desk all day without moving is a ___ habit.","options":["mindful","sedentary","hydrated","moderate"],"answer":"sedentary","explanation":"Well-being vocabulary.","explanation_ar":"مفردات جودة الحياة."},{"q":"Although she had been injured for three months, the gymnast managed to ______ and win a silver medal at the national championship.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["burn out","wind down","bounce back","cut out"],"answer":"bounce back","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."},{"q":"","options":["Close your eyes, you breathe slowly and count to ten.","Close your eyes, breathe slowly and count to ten.","Close your eyes, breathe slowly and you should count to ten.","Closing your eyes, breathe slowly and count to ten."],"answer":"Close your eyes, breathe slowly and count to ten.","explanation":"Imperative – a command or advice.","explanation_ar":"الأمر."},{"q":"","options":["The students designed the garden, and flower planting was done.","The students designed the garden and planted the flowers.","The students designed the garden, and the flowers were planted by them.","The garden was designed by the students, and they planted the flowers by them."],"answer":"The students designed the garden and planted the flowers.","explanation":"Avoid an unnecessary shift in voice.","explanation_ar":"التحوّل في البناء."},{"q":"","options":["If he were more careful, he will make fewer mistakes.","If he were more careful, he makes fewer mistakes.","If he was more careful, he makes fewer mistakes.","If he were more careful, he would make fewer mistakes."],"answer":"If he were more careful, he would make fewer mistakes.","explanation":"Conditional – would / could / might.","explanation_ar":"الشرط."},{"q":"The safety rules require that every worker wear a helmet and ______ the site manager before entering.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["inform","informs","informed","is informing"],"answer":"inform","explanation":"Avoid an unnecessary shift in mood.","explanation_ar":"التحوّل في الصيغة."},{"q":"Which sentence changes from active to passive for no good reason?","options":["The chef prepared the meal and served it at eight.","The chef prepared the meal, and it was served by him at eight.","The chef prepared and served the meal at eight.","The meal was prepared and served at eight."],"answer":"The chef prepared the meal, and it was served by him at eight.","explanation":"Avoid an unnecessary shift in voice.","explanation_ar":"التحوّل في البناء."},{"q":"Regular exercise improves both physical and mental health. ______ people who walk for thirty minutes a day often report better sleep and less stress.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Instead,","For example,","In contrast,","However,"],"answer":"For example,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Sitting for long periods is common for students.\n• A sedentary lifestyle is linked to back pain.\n• Short movement breaks can reduce back pain.\n• Some schools have added two-minute stretching breaks.\n\nThe student wants to explain why some schools have added stretching breaks. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Some schools have added two-minute breaks.","Back pain is a problem for some people.","Because sitting for long periods is linked to back pain, some schools have added short stretching breaks to help students move.","Sitting for long periods is common for students."],"answer":"Because sitting for long periods is linked to back pain, some schools have added short stretching breaks to help students move.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"if i was you, i will cut down on fizzy drinks.\"","options":["If I were you, I will cut down on fizzy drinks.","if I were you, I would cut down on fizzy drinks.","If I was you, I would cut down on fizzy drinks.","If I were you, I would cut down on fizzy drinks."],"answer":"If I were you, I would cut down on fizzy drinks.","explanation":"Subjunctive were – unreal situation.","explanation_ar":"were للمواقف غير الحقيقية."},{"q":"\"The doctor recommended that he rest.\" Why is \"rest\" correct?","options":["After \"recommended that,\" we use the base form (subjunctive).","It is a mistake; it should be \"rests.\"","It is in the past tense.","\"Rest\" is a noun here."],"answer":"After \"recommended that,\" we use the base form (subjunctive).","explanation":"Subjunctive base form after recommend / essential that.","explanation_ar":"المصدر بعد recommend that."},{"q":"Which word has the same meaning as \"relax after a busy time\"?","options":["cope with","burn out","overwhelm","unwind"],"answer":"unwind","explanation":"Well-being vocabulary.","explanation_ar":"مفردات جودة الحياة."}],"theme_ar":"التوازن وجودة الحياة","essential_question_ar":"كيف نحافظ على توازن صحي بين العمل والراحة واللعب؟","can_do":"I can use the indicative, imperative, interrogative, conditional and subjunctive moods, use the subjunctive after verbs like recommend and adjectives like essential, understand well-being idioms and phrasal verbs, and avoid inappropriate shifts in voice and mood.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أستخدم صيغ الإخبار والأمر والاستفهام والشرط والتمني (subjunctive)، وأستخدم صيغة الـ subjunctive بعد أفعال مثل recommend وصفات مثل essential، وأفهم التعابير الاصطلاحية والأفعال المركبة عن جودة الحياة، وأتجنّب التحولات غير المناسبة في البناء والصيغة."});
